{"raw": {"https://vacancies.ntu.ac.uk/Job/JobDetail?JobId=1223": {"title": "Associate Dean, Research", "description": "NTU | Jobs | Search here for your perfect career - Job Information  | Apply for Associate Dean, Research Skip to main content List Vacancies (current) Sign in Accessibility Tools List Vacancies (current) Back to Search Results Associate Dean, Research Apply for job Job reference: 551193 Location: Clifton Campus Employment type: Permanent Contract Team: Academic Admin - School SST Closing date: 15/11/2026 School / Directorate: School of Science and Technology Salary / Grade Management Grade 3 (\u00a390,000 - \u00a3105,000 p.a. pro rata) Where to find us location_on Get directions Diverse community. Inclusive Research. Rewarding Careers. Doing things differently. Associate Dean Research \u00a390,000 - \u00a3105,000 per annum Full time/Permanent About the Role As Associate Dean for Research, in a vibrant and research active school, you will be a highly motivated leader who understands the current research and innovation funding landscape, the value of good communications, networking and the importance of developing an inclusive and forward looking research culture in a vibrant and diverse School of Science and Technology at Nottingham Trent University. You will already be a research leader in your field of international standing with experience of leading, innovating, influencing, facilitating and mentoring as well as in developing strategy, working with senior colleagues within the school and across the university with regards to research and innovation. You will be able to demonstrate your leadership experience in contributing to improved REF outcomes. research impact and outcomes alongside strong leadership skills and a proven ability to initiate, lead, and manage academic teams, departments and projects in a collegiate environment in order to deliver strategic objectives relevant to the School and University. You will be a research leader in your field with strong links to funding bodies, an understanding of the funding landscape and delivery on large scale research projects. You will have an impressive record of world class research outputs and recognition for your professional achievements in a discipline area relevant to the School and the capacity to exercise academic leadership to enhance the standing of the School. You will think rigorously and entrepreneurially about the contributions and future of research within the School and will have a vision for aligning and motivating staff at all levels to achieve the School and University strategic ambitions. You will have experience of networking, collaborating and influencing colleagues to deliver joint projects and achieve stretching goals.. This academic appointment is a permanent post aligned to one or more School disciplines. For more details, please take a look at the role profile. We will consider applications even if you don't meet every single one of the requirements, so don't be put off if you don't match them perfectly. We particularly welcome applications from women and those of a mixed race heritage who are underrepresented in our senior leadership. Interview date: December 2026 About Us The School of Science and Technology at Nottingham Trent University (NTU) is an exciting and inclusive multidisciplinary environment for learning, teaching and research, with some of the best facilities in the UK. We pride ourselves on delivering high-quality teaching and diverse, real-world research. We specialise in biosciences, chemistry, computing and technology, as well as engineering, forensic science, mathematics, physics and sport science. This mix of traditional and modern subjects encourages and inspires future innovators. We are forward thinkers, innovators and challengers of the status quo. We look forward to hearing from you. For informal queries about the role or the team, please contact Professor Kirsty Smallbone (Executive Dean) at Kirsty.smallbone@ntu.ac.uk . Join Us Hybrid working - We support flexible ways of working through a combination of campus-based and home working where applicable. For full-time roles, this includes a minimum of 60% on-campus commitment. We trust colleagues to work with their teams to shape working patterns that enable them to deliver the best possible outcomes for their stakeholders. Flexibility - We welcome and support a range of working patterns and approaches, helping colleagues balance their work and personal commitments while meeting the needs of the role. 35 days annual leave, plus statutory bank holidays and 5 university closure days pro rata. Annual Health Insurance or Private Medical Insurance Salary Sacrifice Retirement Savings Plan with life assurance and income protection. Available to colleagues who choose to opt out of the contractual pension scheme. Minimum colleague contributions of 0% matched with minimum NTU contributions of 8%. Range of health and wellbeing services, including a Health Cash Plan, voluntary benefits, discounts, and savings for all colleagues. Access to a wealth of formal and informal professional development opportunities to develop your skills and advance your career. And a whole lot more\u2026Find out more about the range of benefits we offer. Come and be part of our success. Apply today. Safe and Inclusive At NTU, we continue to build an inclusive culture that encourages, supports and celebrates the diverse voices and experiences of our students and colleagues. By championing positive wellbeing, we promote an environment where all can thrive and reach their full potential. We welcome the unique contributions that you can bring and we encourage people from underrepresented communities and backgrounds to apply to join our team. Depending on your individual circumstances this role may be eligible for sponsorship under the UKVI Skilled Worker route. We recommend that you review your individual circumstances before applying, or for more information visit the Government Skilled Worker visa support page. This role is covered by the Rehabilitation of Offenders Act (1974) and successful applicants will be asked to declare any unspent criminal convictions. Take a look around the company https://www.ntu.ac.uk/ Apply for job favorite_border Save this job Go to main site Terms & Conditions Accessibility Nottingham Trent University\u00a0applicant tracking system delivered and supported by Jobtrain"}, "https://vacancies.ntu.ac.uk/Job/JobDetail?JobId=2587": {"title": "Academic Associate in Computer Science (Part Time Lecturer and Part Time PhD Study)", "description": "NTU | Jobs | Search here for your perfect career - Job Information  | Apply for Academic Associate in Computer Science (Part Time Lecturer and Part Time PhD Study) Skip to main content List Vacancies (current) Sign in Accessibility Tools List Vacancies (current) Back to Search Results Academic Associate in Computer Science (Part Time Lecturer and Part Time PhD Study) Apply for job Job reference: 552552 Location: Clifton Campus Employment type: Fixed Term Contract Team: Computer Science Closing date: 20/11/2026 School / Directorate: School of Science and Technology Salary / Grade Grade G (\u00a333,739 - \u00a338,825 p.a. pro rata) Where to find us location_on Get directions Diverse community. Inclusive Research. Rewarding Careers. Doing things differently. Academic Associate in Computer Science Part Time Lecturer and Part Time PhD Study Grade G (\u00a333,739 - \u00a338,825 p.a. pro rata) 18.5 hours a week, fixed-term for 5 years About the Role The Department of Computer Science at Nottingham Trent University (NTU) is seeking to appoint an enthusiastic and talented Academic Associate in Computer Science. The Academic Associates are expected to contribute to the academic activities of the department ( 0.5 FTE ) and concurrently undertake a part-time doctoral training programme leading towards the award of PhD. The successful post holder will be awarded a contract, which intrinsically links their teaching and learning commitments with their individual research activities. The Academic Associates will be working and completing a PhD in one of the research areas including 1) Computational Intelligence 2) Interactive Systems 3) Pervasive Computing 4) Cognitive Computing 5) Cybersecurity. About Us The Department of Computer Science resides within the School of Science and Technology on the Clifton Campus of NTU and there are excellent collaborative opportunities with colleagues in other departments and research centres. NTU has a long and established history for delivering computing-related programmes. Our Department of Computer Science combines internationally significant research with an outstanding record for teaching excellence. Our state-of-the-art facilities and career-focused approach to course design provide the right conditions for students to excel in their chosen fields. The department has research strengths in Interactive Systems, Computational Intelligence, Pervasive Computing, and Cybersecurity, with active research groups breaking new ground in these fields. Interview w/c 7th December 2026 Join Us Please review the Job Description and Person Specification provided below. If you have any specific queries in relation to this position that the online information does not cover, then please contact: Professor Ahmad Lotfi, Head of Department of Computer Science, via CMPAdmin@ntu.ac.uk If you are interested in this opportunity, alongside the online application, please complete a) a covering letter b) your CV c) a short statement (no more than one side of A4), outlining the topic you wish to research (or a research proposal). You may also identify potential supervisors for your research project. The shortlisted candidates will be required to deliver a 5-minute presentation about their proposed PhD research project. Safe and Inclusive At NTU, we continue to build an inclusive culture that encourages, supports and celebrates the diverse voices and experiences of our students and colleagues. By championing positive wellbeing, we promote an environment where all can thrive and reach their full potential. We welcome the unique contributions that you can bring and we encourage people from underrepresented communities and backgrounds to apply to join our team. Please note that unfortunately, this role has been assessed as ineligible for sponsorship under the UK Visas & Immigration points-based immigration system however, we recommend that you assess your eligibility before applying for this position. For more information visit the Government Skilled Worker visa support page. However, applications are welcome from candidates who do not currently have the right to work in the UK, but who would be eligible to obtain a valid visa via another route. Please consult the Home Office website for further information. Please note that this role is covered by the Rehabilitation of Offenders Act (1974) and successful applicants will be asked to declare any unspent criminal convictions. Take a look around the company https://www.ntu.ac.uk/ Apply for job favorite_border Save this job Go to main site Terms & Conditions Accessibility Nottingham Trent University\u00a0applicant tracking system delivered and supported by Jobtrain"}, "https://vacancies.ntu.ac.uk/Job/JobDetail?JobId=2636": {"title": "Joiner", "description": "NTU | Jobs | Search here for your perfect career - Job Information  | Apply for Joiner Cookie Policy By clicking \"Allow Cookies\", you agree to the storing of cookies on your device to analyse site usage, and assist in our marketing efforts. Cookie Policy (Opens in a new tab) Decline Allow cookies Skip to main content List Vacancies (current) Sign in Accessibility Tools List Vacancies (current) Back to Search Results Joiner Apply for job Job reference: 552601 Location: Clifton Campus Employment type: Permanent Contract Team: Energy, Engineering and Maintenance Closing date: 01/11/2026 School / Directorate: Estates and Campus Services Salary / Grade Grade F (\u00a329,352 - \u00a333,739 p.a. pro rata) Where to find us location_on Get directions Build a Rewarding Career. Doing things differently. Joiner Salary- \u00a329,352 - \u00a333,739 per annum Full time/ permanent Based at Clifton campus About the Role As an NTU Joiner, you will be part of the in-house Estates team that supports and enables the safe, compliant and efficient operation of the university estate. The role is varied and diverse, with day-to-day duties ranging from ensuring that our estate is safe and operational, through to supporting the delivery of key University events such as open days and graduation ceremonies. Typical duties will include: Undertaking of routine joinery repairs and maintenance in all the University buildings. Manufacture and installation of purpose made joinery items. Installation works and supporting the delivery of minor works projects. Supporting the delivery of legislative compliance duties, such as fire door inspections and repairs. Supporting the set up and delivery of key University events such as open days, graduation and clearing. For more details, please take a look at the role profile. We'll still consider applications even if you don't meet every single one of the requirements, so don't be put off if you don't match them perfectly. We're focused on finding the right person for the role. Interview Date: w/c 16th November 2026 About Us Over the past 15 years, we\u2019ve invested more than \u00a3450m across our five campuses in Nottingham and Nottinghamshire. Named \u2018Modern University of the Year 2023\u2019 by The Times and The Sunday Times, we know that our campuses and facilities are a key part of our success, which is why we\u2019re investing a further \u00a3250m across our sites over the next five years. As one of the most environmentally responsible universities in the world, we lead the sector by embedding sustainability into everything we do. As part of our Estates team, you\u2019ll help to guide and support this work by reducing our carbon impact and accelerating our progress to net zero by 2040. Our Estates Our City campus is home to stunning Grade II listed buildings, dynamic architecture and picturesque living walls and terraces. In 2021, our renovation of a former Wesleyan Chapel (University Hall) was recognised as the \u2018University Impact Initiative of the Year\u2019 by the Association for University Directors of Estates (AUDE). We continue to invest in sector leading projects with the construction of the Design and Digital Arts building which will open in 2024. Recent developments at our Clifton campus include a \u00a323m Medical Technology Innovation Facility (MTIF), \u00a315m Health and Allied Professions Centre and \u00a31.6m Smart Wireless Innovation Facility (SWIFT). Our Brackenhurst campus offers a veterinary nursing centre, climate-controlled greenhouses, and multiple state-of-the-art laboratories. The Lyth building was completed in 2020 at a cost of \u00a311.5m and offers a wide range of high-quality teaching and social spaces. Our Confetti campus offers access to professional TV, film and music studios, as well as specialist labs, computer suites, industry-standard tech and world class facilities for Esports. From 2023, Confetti will be launching a second site in Whitechapel London, complete with a multipurpose, live events venue. Located at Vision West Nottinghamshire College, our \u00a36.5m Mansfield Hub opened in 2020 and includes state-of-the-art training facilities for clinical practitioners, as well as a sport science laboratory, lecture theatres and flexible study spaces. For any informal queries about the role or the team, please contact John Greasley, Maintenance Manager at john.greasley@ntu.ac.u Join Us We\u2019ll look after you with ongoing support, good development opportunities and a competitive salary that rewards your contribution. We also offer generous holidays, flexible working options, a pension scheme, great facilities and wide range of savings, discounts and benefits. Find out more about the range of benefits we offer. We are committed to advancing Equality, Diversity and Inclusion across all areas of our work. We actively promote a culture of respect and belonging and we welcome applications from people of all backgrounds. For more information please click here - Equality, Diversity and Inclusion | Nottingham Trent University Start to think about your future differently. Apply here. Safe and Inclusive At NTU, we continue to build an inclusive culture that encourages, supports and celebrates the diverse voices and experiences of our students and colleagues. By championing positive wellbeing, we promote an environment where all can thrive and reach their full potential. We welcome the unique contributions that you can bring and we encourage people from underrepresented communities and backgrounds to apply to join our team. Please note that unfortunately, this role has been assessed as ineligible for sponsorship under the UK Visas & Immigration points-based immigration system however, we recommend that you assess your eligibility before applying for this position. For more information visit the Government Skilled Worker visa support page. However, applications are welcome from candidates who do not currently have the right to work in the UK, but who would be eligible to obtain a valid visa via another route. Please consult the Home Office website for further information. Please note that this role is covered by the Rehabilitation of Offenders Act (1974) and successful applicants will be asked to declare any unspent criminal convictions. Supporting Documents save_alt JDPS- Joiner (PDF, KB) Take a look around the company https://www.ntu.ac.uk/ Apply for job favorite_border Save this job Go to main site Terms & Conditions Accessibility Nottingham Trent University\u00a0applicant tracking system delivered and supported by Jobtrain"}, "https://vacancies.ntu.ac.uk/Job/JobDetail?JobId=2633": {"title": "Electrician", "description": "NTU | Jobs | Search here for your perfect career - Job Information  | Apply for Electrician Cookie Policy By clicking \"Allow Cookies\", you agree to the storing of cookies on your device to analyse site usage, and assist in our marketing efforts. Cookie Policy (Opens in a new tab) Decline Allow cookies Skip to main content List Vacancies (current) Sign in Accessibility Tools List Vacancies (current) Back to Search Results Electrician Apply for job Job reference: 552598 Location: City Campus Employment type: Permanent Contract Team: Energy, Engineering and Maintenance Closing date: 01/11/2026 School / Directorate: Estates and Campus Services Salary / Grade Grade F (\u00a329,352 - \u00a333,739 p.a. pro rata) Where to find us location_on Get directions Build a Rewarding Career. Doing things differently. Electrician x3 positions Salary- \u00a329,352 - \u00a333,739 per annum Full time / permanent Based at City Campus About the Role As an NTU Electrician, you will be part of the in-house Estates team that supports and enables the safe, compliant and efficient operation of the university estate. The role is varied and diverse, with day-to-day duties ranging from ensuring that our estate is safe and operational, through to supporting the delivery of key University events such as open days and graduation ceremonies. Typical duties will include: Undertaking of fault finding, routine maintenance tasks and repairs on Low and Extra Low Voltage systems in all the university buildings. Electrical installation work to new and existing circuits. Supporting the delivery of minor works projects. Undertaking electrical testing. Undertaking statutory inspections on electrical, fire, emergency lighting and control systems. Supporting the set up and delivery of key university events such as open days, graduation and clearing. For more details, please take a look at the role profile. We'll still consider applications even if you don't meet every single one of the requirements, so don't be put off if you don't match them perfectly. We're focused on finding the right person for the role. Interview Date: w/c 16th November 2026 About Us Over the past 15 years, we\u2019ve invested more than \u00a3450m across our five campuses in Nottingham and Nottinghamshire. Named \u2018Modern University of the Year 2023\u2019 by The Times and The Sunday Times, we know that our campuses and facilities are a key part of our success, which is why we\u2019re investing a further \u00a3250m across our sites over the next five years. As one of the most environmentally responsible universities in the world, we lead the sector by embedding sustainability into everything we do. As part of our Estates team, you\u2019ll help to guide and support this work by reducing our carbon impact and accelerating our progress to net zero by 2040. Our Estates Our City campus is home to stunning Grade II listed buildings, dynamic architecture and picturesque living walls and terraces. In 2021, our renovation of a former Wesleyan Chapel (University Hall) was recognised as the \u2018University Impact Initiative of the Year\u2019 by the Association for University Directors of Estates (AUDE). We continue to invest in sector leading projects with the construction of the Design and Digital Arts building which will open in 2024. Recent developments at our Clifton campus include a \u00a323m Medical Technology Innovation Facility (MTIF), \u00a315m Health and Allied Professions Centre and \u00a31.6m Smart Wireless Innovation Facility (SWIFT). Our Brackenhurst campus offers a veterinary nursing centre, climate-controlled greenhouses, and multiple state-of-the-art laboratories. The Lyth building was completed in 2020 at a cost of \u00a311.5m and offers a wide range of high-quality teaching and social spaces. Our Confetti campus offers access to professional TV, film and music studios, as well as specialist labs, computer suites, industry-standard tech and world class facilities for Esports. From 2023, Confetti will be launching a second site in Whitechapel London, complete with a multipurpose, live events venue. Located at Vision West Nottinghamshire College, our \u00a36.5m Mansfield Hub opened in 2020 and includes state-of-the-art training facilities for clinical practitioners, as well as a sport science laboratory, lecture theatres and flexible study spaces. For any informal queries about the role or the team, please contact John Greasley, Maintenance Manager at john.greasley@ntu.ac.u Join Us We\u2019ll look after you with ongoing support, good development opportunities and a competitive salary that rewards your contribution. We also offer generous holidays, flexible working options, a pension scheme, great facilities and wide range of savings, discounts and benefits. Find out more about the range of benefits we offer. We are committed to advancing Equality, Diversity and Inclusion across all areas of our work. We actively promote a culture of respect and belonging and we welcome applications from people of all backgrounds. For more information please click here - Equality, Diversity and Inclusion | Nottingham Trent University Start to think about your future differently. Apply here. Safe and Inclusive At NTU, we continue to build an inclusive culture that encourages, supports and celebrates the diverse voices and experiences of our students and colleagues. By championing positive wellbeing, we promote an environment where all can thrive and reach their full potential. We welcome the unique contributions that you can bring and we encourage people from underrepresented communities and backgrounds to apply to join our team. Please note that unfortunately, this role has been assessed as ineligible for sponsorship under the UK Visas & Immigration points-based immigration system however, we recommend that you assess your eligibility before applying for this position. For more information visit the Government Skilled Worker visa support page. However, applications are welcome from candidates who do not currently have the right to work in the UK, but who would be eligible to obtain a valid visa via another route. Please consult the Home Office website for further information. Please note that this role is covered by the Rehabilitation of Offenders Act (1974) and successful applicants will be asked to declare any unspent criminal convictions. Supporting Documents save_alt JDPS- Electrician (PDF, KB) Take a look around the company https://www.ntu.ac.uk/ Apply for job favorite_border Save this job Go to main site Terms & Conditions Accessibility Nottingham Trent University\u00a0applicant tracking system delivered and supported by Jobtrain"}, "https://vacancies.ntu.ac.uk/Job/JobDetail?JobId=2640": {"title": "Human Resources Advisor", "description": "NTU | Jobs | Search here for your perfect career - Job Information  | Apply for Human Resources Advisor Cookie Policy By clicking \"Allow Cookies\", you agree to the storing of cookies on your device to analyse site usage, and assist in our marketing efforts. Cookie Policy (Opens in a new tab) Decline Allow cookies Skip to main content List Vacancies (current) Sign in Accessibility Tools List Vacancies (current) Back to Search Results Human Resources Advisor Apply for job Job reference: 552605 Location: City Campus Employment type: Permanent Contract Team: HR BP Team Closing date: 25/10/2026 School / Directorate: People Services Salary / Grade Grade G (\u00a333,739 - \u00a338,825 p.a. pro rata) Where to find us location_on Get directions Putting the Human into Resources. Doing things differently. Human Resources Advisor Salary- \u00a333,739 - \u00a338,825 per annum Full time- 37 hours per week/ permanent About the Role Working within the HR Business Partnering team, you'll provide proactive, specialist HR advice to the organisation that supports the timely and effective management of employee relations issues and contributes to the achievement of our strategic aims. You will lead on the provision of specialist employee relations advice and support services to managers on Human Resources operational matters, such as conduct and capability, grievance, attendance management, performance management, colleague retention and redeployment and colleague wellbeing. You'll also provide operational HR support to a range of HR activities and projects to continuously develop and improve the HR service. For more details, please take a look at the role profile. We'll still consider applications even if you don't meet every single one of the requirements, so don't be put off if you don't match them perfectly. To ensure the diverse needs of our team are met we actively encourage secondments and offer flexible part-time working patterns - we're focused on finding the right person for the role. Please take a look at the Job Description below and make particular reference to how you match the Person Specification within your supporting statements. 1st stage interviews: 4th & 6th November 2026- via Microsoft Teams 2nd stage interviews: Monday 16th November 2026 in person About Us Nottingham Trent University is a successful and ambitious university that is recognised for its innovation and inclusivity and being bold enough to do things differently. This is an exciting time to join the HR team focused on \u2018Empowering People\u2019 a key theme in delivering the strategic plan \u2018University, reimagined\u2019. Our HR team is responsible for our NTU colleagues employment needs. We cover a wide range of HR and Organisational Development services, including Health, Safety and Wellbeing, Resourcing and Reward and Recognition. Distinctive and disruptive, we empower people to do the right thing. We are bold in exploring unfamiliar paths and pursuing novel solutions. If you have a passion for making a real difference, joining us in HR at NTU could be the perfect role for you. For any informal queries about the role or the HR team, please contact Tina Bull HR Business Partner at tina.bull@ntu.ac.uk. Join Us Hybrid working - We support flexible ways of working through a combination of campus-based and home working where applicable. For full-time roles, this includes a minimum of 60% on-campus commitment. We trust colleagues to work with their teams to shape working patterns that enable them to deliver the best possible outcomes for their stakeholders. Flexibility - We welcome and support a range of working patterns and approaches, helping colleagues balance their work and personal commitments while meeting the needs of the role. 28 - 30 days annual leave, plus statutory bank holidays and 5 university closure days pro rata. Salary Sacrifice Retirement Savings Plan with life assurance and income protection. Available to colleagues who choose to opt out of the contractual pension scheme. Minimum colleague contributions of 0% matched with minimum NTU contributions of 8%. Local Government Pension Scheme (LGPS) when you enrol NTU contribute 14.8% of your salary Range of health and wellbeing services, including a Health Cash Plan, voluntary benefits, discounts, and savings for all colleagues. Access to a wealth of formal and informal professional development opportunities to develop your skills and advance your career. We are committed to advancing Equality, Diversity and Inclusion across all areas of our work. We actively promote a culture of respect and belonging and we welcome applications from people of all backgrounds. For more information please click here - Equality, Diversity and Inclusion | Nottingham Trent University And a whole lot more\u2026Find out more about the range of benefits we offer. Come and be part of our success. Apply today. Safe and Inclusive At NTU, we continue to build an inclusive culture that encourages, supports and celebrates the diverse voices and experiences of our students and colleagues. By championing positive wellbeing, we promote an environment where all can thrive and reach their full potential. We welcome the unique contributions that you can bring and we encourage people from underrepresented communities and backgrounds to apply to join our team. Please note that unfortunately, this role has been assessed as ineligible for sponsorship under the UK Visas & Immigration points-based immigration system however, we recommend that you assess your eligibility before applying for this position. For more information visit the Government Skilled Worker visa support page. However, applications are welcome from candidates who do not currently have the right to work in the UK, but who would be eligible to obtain a valid visa via another route. Please consult the Home Office website for further information. Please note that this role is covered by the Rehabilitation of Offenders Act (1974) and successful applicants will be asked to declare any unspent criminal convictions. Supporting Documents save_alt JDPS- Human Resources Advisor (PDF, KB) Take a look around the company https://www.ntu.ac.uk/ Apply for job favorite_border Save this job Go to main site Terms & Conditions Accessibility Nottingham Trent University\u00a0applicant tracking system delivered and supported by Jobtrain"}, "https://vacancies.ntu.ac.uk/Job/JobDetail?JobId=2574": {"title": "Technical Specialist", "description": "NTU | Jobs | Search here for your perfect career - Job Information  | Apply for Technical Specialist Skip to main content List Vacancies (current) Sign in Accessibility Tools List Vacancies (current) Back to Search Results Technical Specialist Apply for job Job reference: 552540 Location: Clifton Campus Employment type: Fixed Term Contract Team: Chemistry and Forensics Closing date: 18/10/2026 School / Directorate: School of Science and Technology Salary / Grade Grade G (\u00a333,739 - \u00a338,825 p.a. pro rata) Where to find us location_on Get directions Diverse community. Inclusive Research. Rewarding Careers. Doing things differently. Technical Specialist - Chemistry Salary- \u00a333,739 - \u00a338,825 per annum Full Time/ Fixed Term contract ( 9 Months ) About the Role One exciting vacancy has arisen for a Technical Specialist in Chemistry to manage a suite of research labs.. The role involves working with the chemistry academic team to support undergraduate and masters level teaching and research projects, in the areas of Chemistry and physical science The post holder will be responsible for ensuring that the research labs are kept to the highest standards of Health and Safety, cleanliness, and organisation. Equipment within these spaces will be maintained and demonstrated to students during practical sessions. Training on equipment for research students and junior staff members will also be undertaken. Excellent communication skills are essential to liaise with the academic team to determine technical requirements, manage the workload of the technical team, and to assist students in the labs where required. This is an exciting opportunity for an enthusiastic and motivated individual with relevant experience, either within a higher education/training environment, or industry. Ideally the post holder will have previous managerial experience. You will also be expected to be flexible and support colleagues and students in other areas of the School of Science and Technology, as part of a School-wide technical team. Other essential competencies for the job are organisation, leadership, adaptability, and a commitment to a high-quality customer experience. We are committed to delivering outstanding teaching and world-leading research, that changes lives and society. If you are ambitious to shape the future, and contribute to our mission, come and join our exciting team of enthusiastic staff and students. For more details, please take a look at the role profile. We'll still consider applications even if you don't meet every single one of the requirements, so don't be put off if you don't match them perfectly. Interview Date: w/c 26th October 2026 About Us The School of Science and Technology at Nottingham Trent University (NTU) is an exciting multidisciplinary environment for learning, teaching and research, with some of the best facilities in the UK. We pride ourselves on delivering high-quality teaching and diverse, real-world research. We specialise in biosciences, chemistry, computing and technology, as well as engineering, forensic science, mathematics, physics and sport science. This mix of traditional and modern subjects encourages and inspires future innovators. In the Department of Chemistry, courses are taught in modern, innovative spaces, offering excellent career prospects and accreditation by The Royal Society of Chemistry. The Department has an active research community with a diverse range of knowledge and expertise. For any informal queries about the role or the team, please contact Diego Lo Destro (Technical Team Leader) at diego.lodestro@ntu.ac.uk. Join Us Hybrid working - We support flexible ways of working through a combination of campus-based and home working where applicable. For full-time roles, this includes a minimum of 60% on-campus commitment. We trust colleagues to work with their teams to shape working patterns that enable them to deliver the best possible outcomes for their stakeholders. Flexibility - We welcome and support a range of working patterns and approaches, helping colleagues balance their work and personal commitments while meeting the needs of the role. 28 - 30 days annual leave, plus statutory bank holidays and 5 university closure days pro rata. Salary Sacrifice Retirement Savings Plan with life assurance and income protection. Available to colleagues who choose to opt out of the contractual pension scheme. Minimum colleague contributions of 0% matched with minimum NTU contributions of 8%. Range of health and wellbeing services, including a Health Cash Plan, voluntary benefits, discounts, and savings for all colleagues. Access to a wealth of formal and informal professional development opportunities to develop your skills and advance your career. We are committed to advancing Equality, Diversity and Inclusion across all areas of our work. We actively promote a culture of respect and belonging and we welcome applications from people of all backgrounds. For more information please click here - Equality, Diversity and Inclusion | Nottingham Trent University And a whole lot more\u2026Find out more about the range of benefits we offer. Come and be part of our success. Apply today. Safe and Inclusive At NTU, we continue to build an inclusive culture that encourages, supports and celebrates the diverse voices and experiences of our students and colleagues. By championing positive wellbeing, we promote an environment where all can thrive and reach their full potential. We welcome the unique contributions that you can bring and we encourage people from underrepresented communities and backgrounds to apply to join our team. Please note that unfortunately, this role has been assessed as ineligible for sponsorship under the UK Visas & Immigration points-based immigration system however, we recommend that you assess your eligibility before applying for this position. For more information visit the Government Skilled Worker visa support page. However, applications are welcome from candidates who do not currently have the right to work in the UK, but who would be eligible to obtain a valid visa via another route. Please consult the Home Office website for further information. Please note that this role is covered by the Rehabilitation of Offenders Act (1974) and successful applicants will be asked to declare any unspent criminal convictions. Take a look around the company https://www.ntu.ac.uk/ Apply for job favorite_border Save this job Go to main site Terms & Conditions Accessibility Nottingham Trent University\u00a0applicant tracking system delivered and supported by Jobtrain"}, "https://vacancies.ntu.ac.uk/Job/JobDetail?JobId=2639": {"title": "Lecturer in Paramedicine", "description": "NTU | Jobs | Search here for your perfect career - Job Information  | Apply for Lecturer in Paramedicine Skip to main content List Vacancies (current) Sign in Accessibility Tools List Vacancies (current) Back to Search Results Lecturer in Paramedicine Apply for job Job reference: 552604 Location: Clifton Campus Employment type: Permanent Contract Team: Nottingham Institute of Health and Social Care Closing date: 28/10/2026 School / Directorate: School of Social Sciences Salary / Grade HE Lecturer (\u00a339,984 - \u00a343,671 p.a. pro rata) Where to find us location_on Get directions Inspire, drive change and save lives. Doing things differently. Lecturer in Paramedicine Salary- \u00a339,984 - \u00a343,671 per annum Full time/ permanent About the Role The Nottingham Institute of Health and Social Care at Nottingham Trent University is looking to appoint an enthusiastic and forward-thinking Paramedic Lecturer to join our academic team. We\u2019re seeking an individual who is experienced in the field of Paramedicine and who can provide high quality teaching and learning for our students. The successful candidate will join the Paramedic Team to make a valued contribution to our range of Paramedic, ambulance practice and continuing professional development courses. You will participate in the planning, delivery, assessment, and quality assurance processes across the Paramedic programmes. You will contribute to student recruitment for both the courses. You will act as a personal tutor for Paramedic students and apprentices, providing pastoral care, and coordinating progress reviews for apprentices, working collaboratively with our key stakeholder organisations to ensure support and high-quality learning experiences for students. The successful candidate will have experience working with learners in practice or higher education, designing, and delivering learning opportunities, and have a good understanding of current and evolving clinical, professional, and policy developments in Paramedicine. You will possess excellent communication skills with a willingness to continue developing your scholarly, practice, or research profile. For more details, please take a look at the role profile. We'll still consider applications even if you don't meet every single one of the requirements, so don't be put off if you don't match them perfectly. Interview Date: Thursday 5th November 2026 About Us Nottingham Institute of Health and Social Care brings together expert and enthusiastic staff from across the health, social care, and social work sectors, many of whom are experienced practitioners and recognised leaders in their fields. Our academics are actively engaged in research and scholarship, with work that is widely published and directly informs our curriculum, ensuring students benefit from a contemporary, evidence-based and professionally relevant learning experience. We are committed to providing a vibrant, inclusive and supportive learning environment where teaching is grounded in research, professional practice and a strong commitment to student success. By fostering collaboration between students, practitioners, researchers and external partners, we prepare graduates to make a meaningful impact within their professions and communities. The Institute is dedicated to developing innovative education and research that addresses the challenges facing health and social care services today. Through our strong partnerships with healthcare, social care and community organisations, we strive to make a positive contribution to improving health, wellbeing and social outcomes for all. Our ambition is to equip the next generation of professionals with the knowledge, skills and values needed to lead change and improve lives in an evolving health and social care landscape. For any informal queries about the role or the team, please contact Carl Webster, Principal Lecturer Paramedicine at Carl.Webster@ntu.ac.uk or Anne Felton, Academic Director at Anne.Felton@ntu.ac.uk Join Us Find out more about our academic community at NTU, including the support we offer to academics at all stages of their careers. We also offer: Hybrid working - We support flexible ways of working through a combination of campus-based and home working where applicable. For full-time roles, this includes a minimum of 60% on-campus commitment. We trust colleagues to work with their teams to shape working patterns that enable them to deliver the best possible outcomes for their stakeholders. Flexibility - We welcome and support a range of working patterns and approaches, helping colleagues balance their work and personal commitments while meeting the needs of the role. 30 - 35 days annual leave per year plus statutory bank holidays and 5 university closure days pro rata Salary Sacrifice Retirement Savings Plan with life assurance and income protection. Available to colleagues who choose to opt out of the contractual pension scheme. Minimum colleague contributions of 0% matched with minimum NTU contributions of 8%. Opportunity to receive a bonus for exceptional performance and contribution Range of health and wellbeing services, including a Health Cash Plan, voluntary benefits, discounts, and savings for all colleagues. We are committed to advancing Equality, Diversity and Inclusion across all areas of our work. We actively promote a culture of respect and belonging and we welcome applications from people of all backgrounds. For more information please click here - Equality, Diversity and Inclusion | Nottingham Trent University And a whole lot more\u2026Find out more about the range of benefits we offer. Come and be part of our success. Apply today. Safe and Inclusive At NTU, we continue to build an inclusive culture that encourages, supports and celebrates the diverse voices and experiences of our students and colleagues. By championing positive wellbeing, we promote an environment where all can thrive and reach their full potential. We welcome the unique contributions that you can bring and we encourage people from underrepresented communities and backgrounds to apply to join our team. Please note that unfortunately, this role has been assessed as ineligible for sponsorship under the UK Visas & Immigration points-based immigration system however, we recommend that you assess your eligibility before applying for this position. For more information visit the Government Skilled Worker visa support page. However, applications are welcome from candidates who do not currently have the right to work in the UK, but who would be eligible to obtain a valid visa via another route. Please consult the Home Office website for further information. Please note that this role is covered by the Rehabilitation of Offenders Act (1974) and successful applicants will be asked to declare any unspent criminal convictions. Take a look around the company https://www.ntu.ac.uk/ Apply for job favorite_border Save this job Go to main site Terms & Conditions Accessibility Nottingham Trent University\u00a0applicant tracking system delivered and supported by Jobtrain"}, "https://vacancies.ntu.ac.uk/Job/JobDetail?JobId=2561": {"title": "Information Assistant", "description": "NTU | Jobs | Search here for your perfect career - Job Information  | Apply for Information Assistant Skip to main content List Vacancies (current) Sign in Accessibility Tools List Vacancies (current) Back to Search Results Information Assistant Apply for job Job reference: 552527 Location: Clifton Campus Employment type: Permanent Contract Team: Libraries and Learning Resources Closing date: 18/10/2026 School / Directorate: z.Libraries and Learning Resources Salary / Grade Grade D (\u00a326,336 - \u00a327,434 p.a. pro rata) Where to find us location_on Get directions Creating Welcoming Spaces for Learning, Teaching and Research. Doing things differently. Information Assistant- Clifton Campus Salary- \u00a326,336 - \u00a327,434 per annum (pro rata) This is an Annualised hours contract- 23 hours per week Working pattern: 9am - 2pm Monday & Tuesday 8:45am - 5:15pm Saturday 1:45pm - 7:15pm Sunday During term-time Plus 8 additional summer Saturdays (10am - 2pm) About the Role At the heart of Nottingham Trent University, our libraries inspire and enable independent learning and research. We actively engage with our customers and make a difference. We create an inspiring physical and on-line environment for learning and research. We want to make it easy for people to use our libraries and learning resources. And that's where you come in. We're looking for an Information Assistant to join our friendly and welcoming customer service team. For more details, please take a look at the role profile. We'll still consider applications even if you don't meet every single one of the requirements, so don't be put off if you don't match them perfectly. Interview Date: Wednesday 11th November 2026 What you'll be doing This role isn't just checking and sorting books. You'll be an essential support to customers of our libraries and learning resources to providing practical help and guidance. You'll be the go to person for face-face, telephone and online enquiries and assistance. Supporting customers to get online or how to use software one minute and then identifying and referring specialist enquiries the next. No two days will be the same as you'll work, on a rota basis, completing a variety of tasks. What you'll bring You'll bring your excellent customer service skills and ability to work effectively with a wide range of people. If you've got confidence in using IT systems and experience of supporting customers in a busy service environment, then we'd love to hear from you. For more details, please take a look at the role profile. We'll still consider applications even if you don't meet every single one of the requirements, so don't be put off if you don't match them perfectly. For any informal queries about the role or the LLR team, please contact Grace Carter (User Experience Team Leader) at grace.carter@ntu.ac.uk What we offer We can offer you a career with a difference, as together we shape futures, change lives and create the university of the future. We'll look after you with ongoing support, good development opportunities and a competitive salary that rewards your contribution. We also offer generous holidays, a pension scheme, great facilities and a wide range of savings, discounts and benefits. Come and be part of our success. Apply today. Safe and Inclusive At NTU, we continue to build an inclusive culture that encourages, supports and celebrates the diverse voices and experiences of our students and colleagues. By championing positive wellbeing, we promote an environment where all can thrive and reach their full potential. We welcome the unique contributions that you can bring and we encourage people from underrepresented communities and backgrounds to apply to join our team. Please note that unfortunately, this role has been assessed as ineligible for sponsorship under the UK Visas & Immigration points-based immigration system however, we recommend that you assess your eligibility before applying for this position. For more information visit the Government Skilled Worker visa support page. However, applications are welcome from candidates who do not currently have the right to work in the UK, but who would be eligible to obtain a valid visa via another route. Please consult the Home Office website for further information. Please note that this role is covered by the Rehabilitation of Offenders Act (1974) and successful applicants will be asked to declare any unspent criminal convictions. Take a look around the company https://www.ntu.ac.uk/ Apply for job favorite_border Save this job Go to main site Terms & Conditions Accessibility Nottingham Trent University\u00a0applicant tracking system delivered and supported by Jobtrain"}, "https://vacancies.ntu.ac.uk/Job/JobDetail?JobId=2504": {"title": "Senior Lecturer", "description": "NTU | Jobs | Search here for your perfect career - Job Information  | Apply for Senior Lecturer - Visual Effects (teaching) Skip to main content List Vacancies (current) Sign in Accessibility Tools List Vacancies (current) Back to Search Results Senior Lecturer - Visual Effects (teaching) Apply for job Job reference: 552471 Location: City Campus Employment type: Permanent Contract Team: Design and Digital Arts Closing date: 21/10/2026 School / Directorate: Nottingham School of Art & Design Salary / Grade HE Senior Lecturer (\u00a346,320 - \u00a358,624 p.a. pro rata) Where to find us location_on Get directions Build a Rewarding Career. Doing things differently. Senior Lecturer - Visual Effects (Teaching only) (\u00a346,320 - \u00a358,624 p.a. pro rata) Permanent/Part time post 22.2 hours per week - 3 days a week The core purpose of a Teaching-Focused Lecturer is to make a significant contribution to student success through the delivery of high-quality teaching and learning activities within the school. As a key member of the course team, you will contribute to the delivery of modules and course content, helping to ensure students receive an engaging, inclusive and supportive learning experience. You will also support a range of departmental activities, including student recruitment events, departmental meetings and the provision of pastoral support to students. Working closely with course leadership teams, you will help organise teaching resources effectively and play an active role in implementing enhancements to curriculum design and maintaining the school\u2019s high academic standards and excellent student experience and outcomes. You will bring strong subject knowledge, excellent written and verbal communication skills, and confidence in using a range of digital technologies to support learning and teaching. You will be comfortable working both independently and collaboratively and will contribute positively to teaching-related activities across the school. Above all, you will be passionate about supporting students to achieve their potential and succeed in their studies. For more details, please take a look at the role profile. We'll still consider applications even if you don't meet every single one of the requirements, so don't be put off if you don't match them perfectly. Interview date: TBC About Us Nottingham School of Art & Design is one of the world\u2019s leading art and design schools; we have been influencing, inspiring and innovating for over 175 years. Constantly pushing the boundaries of what\u2019s possible, we\u2019re a diverse community of artists, designers, and creatives at the heart of one of the UK\u2019s most innovative cities. Catalysts of change and new thinking, we nurture the best creative and digital talent. We give our students the freedom to take risks and express their creativity and individuality. We carry out bold, original and daring research. We believe in the power of connectivity, collaborating with creative minds around the globe and working with the creative sector to develop highly employable graduates. We bring different disciplines together to inspire our students to think beyond their passion and make a bigger impact, from sustainability to enterprise and social justice. For any informal queries about the role or the team, please contact Jeremy Moorshead (Principle Lecturer Digital Screen Arts) at jeremy.moorshead@ntu.ac.uk Join Us Find out more about our academic community at NTU, including the support we offer to academics at all stages of their careers. We also offer: 30 - 35 days annual leave per year plus statutory bank holidays and 5 university closure days pro rata Salary Sacrifice Retirement Savings Plan with life assurance and income protection. Available to colleagues who choose to opt out of the contractual pension scheme. Minimum colleague contributions of 0% matched with minimum NTU contributions of 8%. Opportunity to receive a bonus for exceptional performance and contribution Range of health and wellbeing services, including a Health Cash Plan, voluntary benefits, discounts, and savings for all colleagues. We are committed to advancing Equality, Diversity and Inclusion across all areas of our work. We actively promote a culture of respect and belonging and we welcome applications from people of all backgrounds. For more information please click here - Equality, Diversity and Inclusion | Nottingham Trent University And a whole lot more\u2026Find out more about the range of benefits we offer. Come and be part of our success. Apply today. Safe and Inclusive At NTU, we continue to build an inclusive culture that encourages, supports and celebrates the diverse voices and experiences of our students and colleagues. By championing positive wellbeing, we promote an environment where all can thrive and reach their full potential. We welcome the unique contributions that you can bring and we encourage people from underrepresented communities and backgrounds to apply to join our team. Depending on your individual circumstances this role may be eligible for sponsorship under the UKVI Skilled Worker route. We recommend that you review your individual circumstances before applying, or for more information visit the Government Skilled Worker visa support page. This role is covered by the Rehabilitation of Offenders Act (1974) and successful applicants will be asked to declare any unspent criminal convictions. Take a look around the company https://www.ntu.ac.uk/ Apply for job favorite_border Save this job Go to main site Terms & Conditions Accessibility Nottingham Trent University\u00a0applicant tracking system delivered and supported by Jobtrain"}, "https://vacancies.ntu.ac.uk/Job/JobDetail?JobId=2563": {"title": "Research Associate in Law", "description": "NTU | Jobs | Search here for your perfect career - Job Information  | Apply for Research Associate in Law Skip to main content List Vacancies (current) Sign in Accessibility Tools List Vacancies (current) Back to Search Results Research Associate in Law Apply for job Job reference: 552529 Location: City Campus Employment type: Fixed Term Contract Team: Masters and Legal Research Closing date: 06/11/2026 School / Directorate: Nottingham Law School Salary / Grade Grade F (\u00a329,352 - \u00a333,739 p.a. pro rata) Where to find us location_on Get directions Build a Rewarding Career. Doing things differently. Research Associate in Law Salary- \u00a329,352 - \u00a333,739 per annum Full time/Fixed for 12 months About the role Are you looking for an opportunity to develop your research experience while contributing to projects that address important legal and social challenges? As a Research Associate in Law, you will work with academic colleagues across Nottingham Law School. Your work will be varied. Depending on the projects to which you are assigned, you may: search for, review and clearly summarise academic literature, legislation, case law and policy materials; contribute to research reports, journal articles and other publications; help design and undertake qualitative research, which may include interviews, focus groups or document analysis; organise, manage and analyse research data in accordance with ethical and data-protection requirements; undertake horizon-scanning to identify emerging legal, policy and research developments; support colleagues in preparing applications for external research funding; assist with research events and engagement activities; and help communicate research findings to academic, professional and public audiences. You will manage your own agreed tasks while working closely with project leads and other members of the research community based in our three research centres: the Centre for Law, Emerging Technologies and Business, the Centre for Rights and Justice, and the Centre for Legal Education. You may also collaborate with external partners and stakeholders from the public, private and third sectors. This role offers you the opportunity to strengthen your research skills, broaden your knowledge across different areas of law and contribute to research with real-world relevance and impact. You will join a supportive and inclusive research environment in which collaboration, professional development and the exchange of ideas are encouraged. The post is offered on a full-time basis, although consideration will also be given to fractional appointments and job-share arrangements For more details, please take a look at the role profile. We'll still consider applications even if you don't meet every single one of the requirements, so don't be put off if you don't match them perfectly. Interview Date: 19th & 20th November 2026 About Us Nottingham Law School (NLS) is one of the leading providers of academic and professional legal education in the country, with an established record of delivering innovative and transformational courses. We are one of the largest law schools in the UK, offering a range of undergraduate degrees, academic and practitioner taught postgraduate courses and a strong research degrees programme. In addition, our students can gain practical experience volunteering at NLS Legal, our multi-award-winning-teaching law firm, the only on-campus law firm at a UK Law School. Research is central to the School\u2019s mission, enabling our work to make a positive difference to lives and society locally, nationally and globally. We foster a vibrant, inclusive and sustainable research environment, supported by a strong research infrastructure. Our approach is founded on the mutually enriching relationship between excellent academic research, professional practice and legal education. Our researchers produce innovative, impactful and world-leading work, often engaging with cross-disciplinary developments and some of the most significant challenges facing society. These include the rights, safety and security of vulnerable groups; the accountability of public- and private-sector bodies; and the financial and environmental sustainability of the public, private and third sectors. For any informal queries about the role or the team, please contact Professor Jonathan Doak (Associate Dean for Research) at jonathan.doak@ntu.ac.uk. Join Us 30 - 35 days annual leave per year plus statutory bank holidays and 5 university closure days pro rata Hybrid working - we encourage and offer a mixture of office working and working from home. You're empowered to define how you work best for the benefits of your stakeholders. Flexibility - take ownership over how you get your work done. We're open to different working patterns and approaches. Salary Sacrifice Retirement Savings Plan with life assurance and income protection. Available to colleagues who choose to opt out of the contractual pension scheme. Minimum colleague contributions of 0% matched with minimum NTU contributions of 8%. Access to a wealth of formal and informal professional development opportunities to develop your skills and advance your career. Range of health and wellbeing services, including a Health Cash Plan, voluntary benefits, discounts, and savings for all colleagues. And a whole lot more\u2026Find out more about the range of benefits we offer. Come and be part of our success. Apply today. Safe and Inclusive At NTU, we continue to build an inclusive culture that encourages, supports and celebrates the diverse voices and experiences of our students and colleagues. By championing positive wellbeing, we promote an environment where all can thrive and reach their full potential. We welcome the unique contributions that you can bring and we encourage people from underrepresented communities and backgrounds to apply to join our team. Please note that unfortunately, this role has been assessed as ineligible for sponsorship under the UK Visas & Immigration points-based immigration system however, we recommend that you assess your eligibility before applying for this position. For more information visit the Government Skilled Worker visa support page. However, applications are welcome from candidates who do not currently have the right to work in the UK, but who would be eligible to obtain a valid visa via another route. Please consult the Home Office website for further information. Please note that this role is covered by the Rehabilitation of Offenders Act (1974) and successful applicants will be asked to declare any unspent criminal convictions. Take a look around the company https://www.ntu.ac.uk/ Apply for job favorite_border Save this job Go to main site Terms & Conditions Accessibility Nottingham Trent University\u00a0applicant tracking system delivered and supported by Jobtrain"}, "https://vacancies.ntu.ac.uk/Job/JobDetail?JobId=2614": {"title": "Observatory Support Officer", "description": "NTU | Jobs | Search here for your perfect career - Job Information  | Apply for Observatory Support Officer Cookie Policy By clicking \"Allow Cookies\", you agree to the storing of cookies on your device to analyse site usage, and assist in our marketing efforts. Cookie Policy (Opens in a new tab) Decline Allow cookies Skip to main content List Vacancies (current) Sign in Accessibility Tools List Vacancies (current) Back to Search Results Observatory Support Officer Apply for job Job reference: 552579 Location: Clifton Campus Employment type: Hourly Paid/Casual Contract Team: Physics and Maths Closing date: 23/10/2026 School / Directorate: School of Science and Technology Salary / Grade Grade G (\u00a333,739 - \u00a338,825 p.a. pro rata) Where to find us location_on Get directions Diverse Community. Rewarding Career. Doing things differently. Observatory Support Officer Special conditions : A rate of \u00a317.48 will be paid per hour in the role as observatory support officer About the Role The Nottingham Trent University onsite observatory is part of the department of Physical Sciences, one of the School of Science and Technology's five departments, with just below 40 academic colleagues. The observatory supports our work with a variety of observational equipment within Astrophysics across a range of areas including teaching (at foundation, bachelors, and masters levels), research, practice, scholarship and community and commercial engagement. We are seeking to appoint hourly paid Observatory Support Officers that will assist in the delivery of high-quality teaching and learning. Duties will include providing technical support and supervision for activities such as observatory related laboratory supervision, observing sessions, planetarium provision, and problem classes. It will also include delivering small scale outreach events, summer schools, and managing the observatory\u2019s social media presence. Scheduling will acknowledge other academic responsibilities expected for (under-) graduate applicant. Having very good communication skills, the successful applicant must demonstrate commitment to supporting Astronomy teaching (related to working with astronomical equipment) to students within our programmes at FdSc, BSc and Master levels, as well as participants of short courses and summer schools. For more details, please take a look at the profile role. We'll still consider applications even if you don't meet every single one of the requirements, so don't be put off if you don't match them perfectly Application Details: Please remember to submit both a CV as well as a cover letter (or supporting statement) for your application. Interview Date: Interviews will commence in the first week of November. Dr Brown (Observatory coordinator) will be in touch following the submission of your application. Interview Date: w/c 2nd November 2026. About Us The School of Science and Technology at Nottingham Trent University (NTU) is an exciting multidisciplinary environment for learning, teaching and research, with some of the best facilities in the UK. We pride ourselves on delivering high-quality teaching and diverse, real-world research. We specialise in biosciences, chemistry, computing and technology, as well as engineering, forensic science, mathematics, physics and sport science. This mix of traditional and modern subjects encourages and inspires future innovators. Our Physical Sciences department has a strong track record of gaining high-calibre research finding and delivering international impact in areas as diverse as acoustic monitoring of honeybees, art conservation and wastewater treatment. For any informal queries about the role or the team, please contact Dr Daniel Brown (Observatory coordinator) at daniel.brown02@ntu.ac.uk . Join Us We can offer you a career with a difference, as together we shape futures, change lives and create the university of the future. Doing things differently, we empower our people to shape, create and innovate. Whether they\u2019re pushing the boundaries with award-winning research, transforming society through global collaborations or supporting and helping our students to achieve their potential. Join our friendly and diverse community of 4,000 professionals, academics and researchers, and you\u2019ll enjoy the support and ownership you need to perform at your best. A great place to work, we value, respect and care for all our colleagues, providing flexible and competitive rewards and genuine opportunities for career progression. So, take on an exciting new challenge with an ambitious university where progress never stops. Safe and Inclusive At NTU, we continue to build an inclusive culture that encourages, supports and celebrates the diverse voices and experiences of our students and colleagues. By championing positive wellbeing, we promote an environment where all can thrive and reach their full potential. We welcome the unique contributions that you can bring and we encourage people from underrepresented communities and backgrounds to apply to join our team. Please note that unfortunately, this role has been assessed as ineligible for sponsorship under the UK Visas & Immigration points-based immigration system however, we recommend that you assess your eligibility before applying for this position. For more information visit the Government Skilled Worker visa support page. However, applications are welcome from candidates who do not currently have the right to work in the UK, but who would be eligible to obtain a valid visa via another route. Please consult the Home Office website for further information. Please note that this role is covered by the Rehabilitation of Offenders Act (1974) and successful applicants will be asked to declare any unspent criminal convictions. Safeguarding Statement Nottingham Trent University is committed to safeguarding and promoting the welfare of young people and expects all colleagues to share this commitment. If you are successful, you will be required to undertake an enhanced application and a Disclosure and Barring Service (DBS) check. The post for which you are applying is exempt from Section 4(2) of the Rehabilitation of Offenders Act 1974 requiring any spent convictions to be declared. Any information you provide will be treated in confidence and only used when considering your suitability for the post. Before you apply we recommend you ensure you are able to supply the documentation listed on the DBS website Supporting Documents save_alt JDPS- Observatory Support Officer (PDF, KB) Take a look around the company https://www.ntu.ac.uk/ Apply for job favorite_border Save this job Go to main site Terms & Conditions Accessibility Nottingham Trent University\u00a0applicant tracking system delivered and supported by Jobtrain"}, "https://vacancies.ntu.ac.uk/Job/JobDetail?JobId=2381": {"title": "Admissions Associate", "description": "NTU | Jobs | Search here for your perfect career - Job Information  | Apply for Admissions Associate Skip to main content List Vacancies (current) Sign in Accessibility Tools List Vacancies (current) Back to Search Results Admissions Associate Apply for job Job reference: 552349 Location: City Campus Employment type: Fixed Term Contract Team: Admissions Closing date: 16/10/2026 School / Directorate: Communications, Alumni Relations, Marketing and Student Recruitment Salary / Grade Grade E (\u00a328,063 - \u00a330,185 p.a. pro rata) Where to find us location_on Get directions Be part of something bigger. Doing things differently. Admissions Associate Grade E (\u00a328,063 - \u00a330,185 p.a. pro rata) 12 Months - Fixed Term Contract About the Role Join our Admissions team and play a key role in shaping the journey of future students. As an Admissions Associate, you\u2019ll support the processing of both undergraduate and postgraduate applications, delivering a fast, fair and high-quality service that makes a real difference to applicants and colleagues across the University. We\u2019re looking for someone who is detail-focused, proactive, and thrives in a fast-paced environment. If you enjoy working to targets, solving problems, and putting the customer at the centre of everything you do, we want to hear from you. In this role, you\u2019ll be: Processing applications accurately and efficiently, meeting KPIs and service standards Delivering a seamless, supportive experience for applicants from start to finish Contributing to a fair, inclusive and transparent admissions process Supporting key University events, including Open Days, Confirmation, Clearing and Graduation Ensuring full compliance with key regulations, including GDPR and data confidentiality For more details, please take a look at the role profile. We'll still consider applications even if you don't meet every single one of the requirements, so don't be put off if you don't match them perfectly. The Admissions team currently operates a hybrid working model, with colleagues typically based three days per week in our Nottingham city centre office and working remotely for the remainder. Please note that this arrangement may vary, and you may be required to attend the office more frequently at times, particularly for meetings, events, Confirmation, Clearing, and team away days. Interviews; w/c 2nd November 2026 About Us Our award-winning Department of Communications, Alumni Relations, Marketing and Student Recruitment (CAMS) is responsible for engaging with key audiences including prospective students to support NTU\u2019s student recruitment targets and driving forward NTU\u2019s reputation and brand. CAMS comprises admissions, applicant engagement, student recruitment events and outreach, international student recruitment, marketing and campaigns, content management, creative services, social media, web and digital, public relations and internal and external communications. If you have a passion for student recruitment, marketing and communications and a drive to make a real difference, CAMS at NTU could be the perfect place for you. In return, CAMS can offer you a culture of positivity, encouragement and mutual support. The senior leadership team are committed to nurturing talent and helping people reach their full potential. But most of all, CAMS believe in change and growth; in daring to do things differently. For any informal queries about the role or the team, please contact Hannah Thornley (Admissions Manager) at Hannah.Thornley@ntu.ac.uk Join Us Hybrid working - We support flexible ways of working through a combination of campus-based and home working where applicable. For full-time roles, this includes a minimum of 60% on-campus commitment. We trust colleagues to work with their teams to shape working patterns that enable them to deliver the best possible outcomes for their stakeholders. Flexibility - We welcome and support a range of working patterns and approaches, helping colleagues balance their work and personal commitments while meeting the needs of the role. 28 - 30 days annual leave, plus statutory bank holidays and 5 university closure days pro rata. Salary Sacrifice Retirement Savings Plan with life assurance and income protection. Available to colleagues who choose to opt out of the contractual pension scheme. Minimum colleague contributions of 0% matched with minimum NTU contributions of 8%. Range of health and wellbeing services, including a Health Cash Plan, voluntary benefits, discounts, and savings for all colleagues. Access to a wealth of formal and informal professional development opportunities to develop your skills and advance your career. We are committed to advancing Equality, Diversity and Inclusion across all areas of our work. We actively promote a culture of respect and belonging and we welcome applications from people of all backgrounds. For more information please click here - Equality, Diversity and Inclusion | Nottingham Trent University And a whole lot more\u2026Find out more about the range of benefits we offer. Come and be part of our success. Apply today. Safe & Inclusive At NTU, we continue to build an inclusive culture that encourages, supports and celebrates the diverse voices and experiences of our students and colleagues. By championing positive wellbeing, we promote an environment where all can thrive and reach their full potential. We welcome the unique contributions that you can bring and we encourage people from underrepresented communities and backgrounds to apply to join our team. Please note that unfortunately, this role has been assessed as ineligible for sponsorship under the UK Visas & Immigration points-based immigration system however, we recommend that you assess your eligibility before applying for this position. For more information visit the Government Skilled Worker visa support page. However, applications are welcome from candidates who do not currently have the right to work in the UK, but who would be eligible to obtain a valid visa via another route. Please consult the Home Office website for further information. Please note that this role is covered by the Rehabilitation of Offenders Act (1974) and successful applicants will be asked to declare any unspent criminal convictions. Take a look around the company https://www.ntu.ac.uk/ Apply for job favorite_border Save this job Go to main site Terms & Conditions Accessibility Nottingham Trent University\u00a0applicant tracking system delivered and supported by Jobtrain"}, "https://vacancies.ntu.ac.uk/Job/JobDetail?JobId=2488": {"title": "Catering Assistant", "description": "NTU | Jobs | Search here for your perfect career - Job Information  | Apply for Catering Assistant Skip to main content List Vacancies (current) Sign in Accessibility Tools List Vacancies (current) Back to Search Results Catering Assistant Apply for job Job reference: 552455 Location: City Campus Employment type: Permanent Contract Team: Events and Hospitality Closing date: 16/10/2026 School / Directorate: z.Campus Operations Salary / Grade Grade OSE (\u00a325,086 p.a. pro rata) Where to find us location_on Get directions Support our students at every stage of their journey. Doing things differently. Catering Assistant \u00a325,086 per annum Full Time/Permanent 5 days over 7, including evenings, weekends and occasional events as required Are you someone who enjoys working with people and takes pride in delivering great hospitality? As a Catering Assistant at Nottingham Trent University, you'll be part of NTU's catering team, delivering hospitality across meetings, conferences, events, and university functions. We are looking for a professional, enthusiastic and customer-focused Catering assistant to join our busy hospitality team on a full-time contract of 37 hours per week, working 5 days out of 7 on a rota basis. This is an exciting opportunity for an individual who is passionate about delivering exceptional customer service across a variety of hospitality settings, including formal dining, banqueting, events and delivered hospitality services. About the Role As a catering assistant, you will play a key role in creating outstanding experiences for our customers. Working across multiple hospitality venues and events, you will be responsible for delivering high-quality food and beverage service, anticipating customer needs and ensuring the highest standards of presentation and professionalism are maintained at all times. The successful candidate will be comfortable working in a fast-paced environment, supporting colleagues as part of a team or without supervision, leading by example and helping to ensure smooth day-to-day operations. For more details, please take a look at the job description. We'll still consider applications even if you don't meet every single one of the requirements, so don't be put off if you don't match them perfectly. Location: This role supports catering operations across Nottingham Trent University's City, Clifton, Brackenhurst, Mansfield, and Confetti campuses, so flexibility to work across different locations is essential. Interview date: W/C 19th October 2026 About Us Nottingham Trent University is a successful and ambitious university that is recognised for its innovation and inclusivity and being bold enough to do things differently. Our Campus Operations team work tirelessly behind the scenes to support our students. Whether you're making sure our students are safe, serving up delicious meals, or ensuring every package reaches its destination, your role matters. Our team's dedication ensures smooth operations, safety, and exceptional experiences. For any informal queries about the role or the Campus Operations team, please contact Gareth Worth at gareth.worth@ntu.ac.uk Join Us Be part of a supportive and dynamic team \u2014help deliver outstanding service and hospitality in a vibrant, on-site environment. Salary Sacrifice Retirement Savings Plan with life assurance and income protection. Available to colleagues who choose to opt out of the contractual pension scheme. Minimum colleague contributions of 0% matched with minimum NTU contributions of 8%. Range of health and wellbeing services, voluntary benefits, discounts, and savings for all colleagues. Access to a wealth of formal and informal professional development opportunities to develop your skills and advance your career. And a whole lot more\u2026 Come and be part of our success. Apply today! Safe & Inclusive At NTU, we continue to build an inclusive culture that encourages, supports and celebrates the diverse voices and experiences of our students and colleagues. We welcome the unique contributions that you can bring and we encourage people from underrepresented communities and backgrounds to apply to join our team. Please note that unfortunately, this role has been assessed as ineligible for sponsorship under the UK Visas & Immigration points-based immigration system, upcoming immigration rules (4th April 2024) changes may impact on eligibility for sponsorship, we recommend that you assess your eligibility before applying for this position. Visit https://www.gov.uk/skilled-worker-visa for more information. However, applications are welcome from candidates who do not currently have the right to work in the UK, but who would be eligible to obtain a valid visa via another route. Please consult the Home Office website for further information. Please note that this role is covered by the Rehabilitation of Offenders Act (1974) and successful applicants will be asked to declare any unspent criminal convictions. Take a look around the company https://www.ntu.ac.uk/ Apply for job favorite_border Save this job Go to main site Terms & Conditions Accessibility Nottingham Trent University\u00a0applicant tracking system delivered and supported by Jobtrain"}, "https://vacancies.ntu.ac.uk/Job/JobDetail?JobId=2656": {"title": "Network Coordinator", "description": "NTU | Jobs | Search here for your perfect career - Job Information  | Apply for Network Coordinator Skip to main content List Vacancies (current) Sign in Accessibility Tools List Vacancies (current) Back to Search Results Network Coordinator Apply for job Job reference: 552621 Location: Clifton Campus Employment type: Fixed Term Contract Team: Computer Science Closing date: 19/10/2026 School / Directorate: School of Science and Technology Salary / Grade Grade G (\u00a333,739 - \u00a338,825 p.a. pro rata) Where to find us location_on Get directions Be part of something bigger. Doing things differently. Network Coordinator- EPSRC Green+ Network Salary- \u00a333,739 - \u00a338,825 per annum Full time/ Fixed term contract for 12 months Important Information: This is an in-person post based in Nottingham. It involves collaboration with other EPSRC-funded networks and international partners. The role requires regular travel across the UK and abroad to support workshops, co-creation activities, tutorials, Hackathons and national level events. About GREEN+ GREEN+ is a national network funded by UKRI through EPSRC. It brings together researchers, green-space providers, healthcare professionals, community organisations and technology developers to explore how AI, sensing and low-energy digital technologies can support physical activity, mental wellbeing and social connectedness in green environments. The Network is led by Professor Eiman Kanjo at Nottingham Trent University, with co-lead Professor Kia Nazarpour at the University of Edinburgh. Role overview We are seeking a proactive and service-focused Network Coordinator to provide reliable operational, administrative and project support to the Network Lead and leadership team. The postholder will help deliver agreed priorities and activities, using initiative to complete assigned work, identify issues and propose improvements within the Network\u2019s strategic direction. Key responsibilities Coordinate the Network\u2019s day-to-day administration and operations. Support events, workshops, sandpits, training, meetings and community-engagement activities. Take responsibility for coordinating and delivering agreed activities, with opportunities to lead specific activities under the direction of the Network Lead. Maintain project plans, records, reports, budgets and stakeholder communications. Liaise with researchers, green-space providers, healthcare professionals, community organisations, industry, government and international partners. Support Network calls, feasibility projects, funding bids, partnerships, laboratories and related academic or institutional initiatives. Provide responsive support to the Network Lead, leadership team and wider consortium. Learn new skills and use AI and digital tools to improve project delivery. Undertake other reasonable duties consistent with the role\u2019s purpose and grade as priorities develop. This is a full-time, 12-month fixed-term post, with the possibility of extension subject to continued funding, performance and operational requirements. Regular workplace attendance and occasional UK or international travel may be required. Further information is available at https://greenplus.uk Please refer to the attached job description and person specification for full details. Interview date: TBC About Us The School of Science and Technology at Nottingham Trent University (NTU) is an exciting multidisciplinary environment for learning, teaching and research, with some of the best facilities in the UK. We pride ourselves on delivering high-quality teaching and diverse, real-world research. We specialise in biosciences, chemistry, computing and technology, as well as engineering, forensic science, mathematics, physics and sport science. This mix of traditional and modern subjects encourages and inspires future innovators. Our Department of Computer Science combines internationally-significant research with an outstanding record for teaching excellence. Our state-of-the-art facilities and career-focused approach to course design provide the right conditions for students to excel in their chosen fields. For any informal queries about the role or the team, please contact Prof. Eiman Kanjo Head of Smart Sensing Lab at eiman.kanjo@ntu.ac.uk Join Us Hybrid working - We support flexible ways of working through a combination of campus-based and home working where applicable. For full-time roles, this includes a minimum of 60% on-campus commitment. We trust colleagues to work with their teams to shape working patterns that enable them to deliver the best possible outcomes for their stakeholders. Flexibility - We welcome and support a range of working patterns and approaches, helping colleagues balance their work and personal commitments while meeting the needs of the role. 28 - 30 days annual leave, plus statutory bank holidays and 5 university closure days pro rata. Salary Sacrifice Retirement Savings Plan with life assurance and income protection. Available to colleagues who choose to opt out of the contractual pension scheme. Minimum colleague contributions of 0% matched with minimum NTU contributions of 8%. Range of health and wellbeing services, including a Health Cash Plan, voluntary benefits, discounts, and savings for all colleagues. Access to a wealth of formal and informal professional development opportunities to develop your skills and advance your career. We are committed to advancing Equality, Diversity and Inclusion across all areas of our work. We actively promote a culture of respect and belonging and we welcome applications from people of all backgrounds. For more information please click here - Equality, Diversity and Inclusion | Nottingham Trent University And a whole lot more\u2026Find out more about the range of benefits we offer. Come and be part of our success. Apply today. Safe and Inclusive At NTU, we continue to build an inclusive culture that encourages, supports and celebrates the diverse voices and experiences of our students and colleagues. By championing positive wellbeing, we promote an environment where all can thrive and reach their full potential. We welcome the unique contributions that you can bring and we encourage people from underrepresented communities and backgrounds to apply to join our team. Please note that unfortunately, this role has been assessed as ineligible for sponsorship under the UK Visas & Immigration points-based immigration system however, we recommend that you assess your eligibility before applying for this position. For more information visit the Government Skilled Worker visa support page. However, applications are welcome from candidates who do not currently have the right to work in the UK, but who would be eligible to obtain a valid visa via another route. Please consult the Home Office website for further information. Please note that this role is covered by the Rehabilitation of Offenders Act (1974) and successful applicants will be asked to declare any unspent criminal convictions. Take a look around the company https://www.ntu.ac.uk/ Apply for job favorite_border Save this job Go to main site Terms & Conditions Accessibility Nottingham Trent University\u00a0applicant tracking system delivered and supported by Jobtrain"}, "https://vacancies.ntu.ac.uk/Job/JobDetail?JobId=2498": {"title": "Senior Technician", "description": "NTU | Jobs | Search here for your perfect career - Job Information  | Apply for Senior Technician Skip to main content List Vacancies (current) Sign in Accessibility Tools List Vacancies (current) Back to Search Results Senior Technician Apply for job Job reference: 552465 Location: Clifton Campus Employment type: Permanent Contract Team: Biosciences Closing date: 25/10/2026 School / Directorate: School of Science and Technology Salary / Grade Grade F (\u00a329,352 - \u00a333,739 p.a. pro rata) Where to find us location_on Get directions Diverse community. Inclusive Research. Rewarding Careers. Doing things differently. Senior Technician Salary- \u00a329,352 - \u00a333,739 per annum Full time/Permanent About the Role As a member of the technical team, you will be expected to demonstrate equipment and techniques and provide support and guidance to students in Bioscience teaching and research laboratories. You will create a positive, industry-relevant learning environment and maintain a safe working environment and escalate issues where necessary. Provide technical support and guidance to academic colleagues in laboratories, workshops, and studios. Ensure all staff and students are working within a safe environment and escalate issues where necessary. Identify appropriate personal development opportunities and actively keep up to date with relevant discipline knowledge, trends, and technology, and apply this learning to practices. Connect with relevant internal and external networks and use these contacts to enhance delivery. Be a team player and support others in creating a positive environment. Interview Date: w/c 09/11/2026 About Us The School of Science and Technology at Nottingham Trent University (NTU) is an exciting multidisciplinary environment for learning, teaching and research, with some of the best facilities in the UK. We pride ourselves on delivering high-quality teaching and diverse, real-world research. We specialise in biosciences, chemistry, computing and technology, as well as engineering, forensic science, mathematics, physics and sport science. This mix of traditional and modern subjects encourages and inspires future innovators. Our courses in the Department of Biosciences are research-led, providing students with cutting-edge knowledge and access to high-specification facilities. It is one of the many reasons why our courses are accredited by the Institute of Biomedical Science, the Royal Society of Biology and the Chartered Institute of Ecology and Environment Management. For any informal queries about the role or the team, please contact Macsen Fryer (Technical Team Leader) at Macsen.Fryer@ntu.ac.uk. Join Us Hybrid working - We support flexible ways of working through a combination of campus-based and home working where applicable. For full-time roles, this includes a minimum of 60% on-campus commitment. We trust colleagues to work with their teams to shape working patterns that enable them to deliver the best possible outcomes for their stakeholders. Flexibility - We welcome and support a range of working patterns and approaches, helping colleagues balance their work and personal commitments while meeting the needs of the role. 28 - 30 days annual leave, plus statutory bank holidays and 5 university closure days pro rata. Salary Sacrifice Retirement Savings Plan with life assurance and income protection. Available to colleagues who choose to opt out of the contractual pension scheme. Minimum colleague contributions of 0% matched with minimum NTU contributions of 8%. Range of health and wellbeing services, including a Health Cash Plan, voluntary benefits, discounts, and savings for all colleagues. Access to a wealth of formal and informal professional development opportunities to develop your skills and advance your career. We are committed to advancing Equality, Diversity and Inclusion across all areas of our work. We actively promote a culture of respect and belonging and we welcome applications from people of all backgrounds. For more information please click here - Equality, Diversity and Inclusion | Nottingham Trent University And a whole lot more\u2026Find out more about the range of benefits we offer. Come and be part of our success. Apply today. Safe and Inclusive At NTU, we continue to build an inclusive culture that encourages, supports and celebrates the diverse voices and experiences of our students and colleagues. By championing positive wellbeing, we promote an environment where all can thrive and reach their full potential. We welcome the unique contributions that you can bring and we encourage people from underrepresented communities and backgrounds to apply to join our team. Please note that unfortunately, this role has been assessed as ineligible for sponsorship under the UK Visas & Immigration points-based immigration system however, we recommend that you assess your eligibility before applying for this position. For more information visit the Government Skilled Worker visa support page. However, applications are welcome from candidates who do not currently have the right to work in the UK, but who would be eligible to obtain a valid visa via another route. Please consult the Home Office website for further information. Please note that this role is covered by the Rehabilitation of Offenders Act (1974) and successful applicants will be asked to declare any unspent criminal convictions. Take a look around the company https://www.ntu.ac.uk/ Apply for job favorite_border Save this job Go to main site Terms & Conditions Accessibility Nottingham Trent University\u00a0applicant tracking system delivered and supported by Jobtrain"}, "https://vacancies.ntu.ac.uk/Job/JobDetail?JobId=2630": {"title": "Lecturer/ Senior Lecturer in Criminal Law", "description": "NTU | Jobs | Search here for your perfect career - Job Information  | Apply for Lecturer/ Senior Lecturer in Criminal Law Skip to main content List Vacancies (current) Sign in Accessibility Tools List Vacancies (current) Back to Search Results Lecturer/ Senior Lecturer in Criminal Law Apply for job Job reference: 552595 Location: City Campus Employment type: Permanent Contract Team: Vocational and Professional Programmes Closing date: 18/10/2026 School / Directorate: Nottingham Law School Salary / Grade HE Lecturer or Senior Lecturer (\u00a339,984 - \u00a358,624 pa pro rata) Where to find us location_on Get directions Shape the Legal Minds of Tomorrow. Doing things differently. Lecturer or Senior Lecturer in Criminal Law Lecturer salary- \u00a339,984 - \u00a343,671 per annum Senior Lecturer salary- \u00a346,320 - \u00a358,624 per annum Full time/Permanent About the Role We are looking to appoint a Lecturer or Senior Lecturer (depending on experience) to teach on\u202four undergraduate and postgraduate (including practitioner) courses. We welcome applications in the area of Criminal Law. You must hold a professional qualification as any of the following: a solicitor or barrister a chartered legal executive (FCILEX) a trade mark attorney or a patent attorney in the jurisdiction of England and Wales If you are in the early stages of an academic career and are considering joining NTU, then our Early Career Academic Development Programme could be just right for you. If you are considering joining NTU as a Senior Lecturer you will benefit from our Senior Lecturer Career Framework , which recognises and rewards you based on your performance, contribution and achievement, and offers the opportunity of faster salary progression compared to the industry\u202faverage. Interview date: 29th October 2026 About Us Nottingham Law School (NLS) is one of the leading providers of academic and professional legal education in the country, with an established record of delivering innovative and transformational courses. We are one of the largest law schools in the UK, offering a range of undergraduate degrees, academic and practitioner taught postgraduate courses and a strong research degrees programme. Our School has built a reputation for excellence in the provision of legal education and in shaping the careers of solicitors, barristers and legal practitioners at both national and international levels. In addition to our outstanding research expertise, we have long established links with policy makers, professional bodies and leading law firms, including a growing number of significant international associations. We have an extensive record of delivering excellent bespoke training programmes for practitioners and professional bodies, and have strengths in commissioned research, both in the UK and overseas. For any informal queries about the role or the team, please contact Elyse Wakelin at elyse.wakelin02@ntu.ac.uk or Alexandra Kastrinou at alexandra.kastrinou@ntu.ac.uk . Join Us Find out more about our academic community at NTU, including the support we offer to academics at all stages of their careers. We also offer: Hybrid working - We support flexible ways of working through a combination of campus-based and home working where applicable. For full-time roles, this includes a minimum of 60% on-campus commitment. We trust colleagues to work with their teams to shape working patterns that enable them to deliver the best possible outcomes for their stakeholders. Flexibility - We welcome and support a range of working patterns and approaches, helping colleagues balance their work and personal commitments while meeting the needs of the role. 30 - 35 days annual leave per year plus statutory bank holidays and 5 university closure days pro rata Salary Sacrifice Retirement Savings Plan with life assurance and income protection. Available to colleagues who choose to opt out of the contractual pension scheme. Minimum colleague contributions of 0% matched with minimum NTU contributions of 8%. Opportunity to receive a bonus for exceptional performance and contribution Range of health and wellbeing services, including a Health Cash Plan, voluntary benefits, discounts, and savings for all colleagues. We are committed to advancing Equality, Diversity and Inclusion across all areas of our work. We actively promote a culture of respect and belonging and we welcome applications from people of all backgrounds. For more information please click here - Equality, Diversity and Inclusion | Nottingham Trent University And a whole lot more\u2026Find out more about the range of benefits we offer. Come and be part of our success. Apply today. Safe and Inclusive At NTU, we continue to build an inclusive culture that encourages, supports and celebrates the diverse voices and experiences of our students and colleagues. By championing positive wellbeing, we promote an environment where all can thrive and reach their full potential. We welcome the unique contributions that you can bring and we encourage people from underrepresented communities and backgrounds to apply to join our team. Depending on your individual circumstances this role may be eligible for sponsorship under the UKVI Skilled Worker route. We recommend that you review your individual circumstances before applying, or for more information visit the Government Skilled Worker visa support page. This role is covered by the Rehabilitation of Offenders Act (1974) and successful applicants will be asked to declare any unspent criminal convictions. Take a look around the company https://www.ntu.ac.uk/ Apply for job favorite_border Save this job Go to main site Terms & Conditions Accessibility Nottingham Trent University\u00a0applicant tracking system delivered and supported by Jobtrain"}, "https://vacancies.ntu.ac.uk/Job/JobDetail?JobId=2611": {"title": "HPL Property Management &amp; Development", "description": "NTU | Jobs | Search here for your perfect career - Job Information  | Apply for HPL Property Management &amp; Development Cookie Policy By clicking \"Allow Cookies\", you agree to the storing of cookies on your device to analyse site usage, and assist in our marketing efforts. Cookie Policy (Opens in a new tab) Decline Allow cookies Skip to main content List Vacancies (current) Sign in Accessibility Tools List Vacancies (current) Back to Search Results HPL Property Management & Development Apply for job Job reference: 552576 Location: City Campus Employment type: Hourly Paid/Casual Contract Team: Property Management and Development Closing date: 31/07/2027 School / Directorate: School of Architecture, Design and the Built Environment Salary / Grade HPL1 (\u00a339,984- \u00a344,977 p.a. pro rata) Where to find us location_on Get directions Build a Rewarding Career. Doing things differently. Hourly Paid Lecturer \u2013 Property Management & Development \u00a3Salary per direct teaching hour. Include any details here specific to role e.g. Length of contract if fixed term This includes 2 or more of the following elements: teaching, preparation and marking of the scheduled programme of work. A flat rate of \u00a3Salary per direct teaching hour will be paid for completing one of the above elements of the schedule. The number of hours required and the days of the week may vary. About the Role To support the delivery of the undergraduate and/or postgraduate portfolio within Property Management & Development by making a direct contribution to teaching. The role will encompass all of the following, but the balance of duties and responsibilities will be determined in discussion with the post holder\u2019s line manager: Subject Area Real Estate Building Surveying Valuation Property Management Law Economics Property Development Planning Construction For more details, please take a look at the role profile. We'll still consider applications even if you don't meet every single one of the requirements, so don't be put off if you don't match them perfectly. To ensure the diverse needs of our team are met we actively encourage secondments and offer flexible part-time working patterns - we're focused on finding the right person for the role. About Us We are the School of Architecture, Design and the Built Environment (ADBE) at Nottingham Trent University. We make, create, design and build. We\u2019re planners and problem solvers. We draw lines, and we break boundaries. We are 3,000 students, five departments and one school. In the School of Architecture, Design and the Built Environment, we stand half way between science and philosophy; and between tradition and disruption. We embrace theoretical rigour and insist on providing hands-on experience for all our students. We celebrate design heritage, and we invite innovation. We\u2019re a nationally renowned stage for talent in making and design. We investigate the physicality of tools and tech, glass and grass, and bricks and mortar. We also explore the abstract excitement of ideas and creative philosophies. For any informal queries about the role or the ADBE team, please contact Keith Lown, Head of Property Management & Development at keith.lown@ntu.ac.uk Join Us Find out more about our academic community at NTU, including the support we offer to academics at all stages of their careers. We also offer: Hybrid working - We support flexible ways of working through a combination of campus-based and home working where applicable. For full-time roles, this includes a minimum of 60% on-campus commitment. We trust colleagues to work with their teams to shape working patterns that enable them to deliver the best possible outcomes for their stakeholders. Flexibility - We welcome and support a range of working patterns and approaches, helping colleagues balance their work and personal commitments while meeting the needs of the role. 30 - 35 days annual leave per year plus statutory bank holidays and 5 university closure days pro rata Salary Sacrifice Retirement Savings Plan with life assurance and income protection. Available to colleagues who choose to opt out of the contractual pension scheme. Minimum colleague contributions of 0% matched with minimum NTU contributions of 8%. Opportunity to receive a bonus for exceptional performance and contribution Range of health and wellbeing services, including a Health Cash Plan, voluntary benefits, discounts, and savings for all colleagues. We are committed to advancing Equality, Diversity and Inclusion across all areas of our work. We actively promote a culture of respect and belonging and we welcome applications from people of all backgrounds. For more information please click here - Equality, Diversity and Inclusion | Nottingham Trent University And a whole lot more\u2026Find out more about the range of benefits we offer. Come and be part of our success. Apply today. Safe and Inclusive At NTU, we continue to build an inclusive culture that encourages, supports and celebrates the diverse voices and experiences of our students and colleagues. By championing positive wellbeing, we promote an environment where all can thrive and reach their full potential. We welcome the unique contributions that you can bring and we encourage people from underrepresented communities and backgrounds to apply to join our team. Please note that unfortunately, this role has been assessed as ineligible for sponsorship under the UK Visas & Immigration points-based immigration system however, we recommend that you assess your eligibility before applying for this position. For more information visit the Government Skilled Worker visa support page. However, applications are welcome from candidates who do not currently have the right to work in the UK, but who would be eligible to obtain a valid visa via another route. Please consult the Home Office website for further information. Please note that this role is covered by the Rehabilitation of Offenders Act (1974) and successful applicants will be asked to declare any unspent criminal convictions. Supporting Documents save_alt 552576 - Hourly Paid Lecturer Property Management and Development JDPS (PDF, KB) Take a look around the company https://www.ntu.ac.uk/ Apply for job favorite_border Save this job Go to main site Terms & Conditions Accessibility Nottingham Trent University\u00a0applicant tracking system delivered and supported by Jobtrain"}, "https://vacancies.ntu.ac.uk/Job/JobDetail?JobId=2547": {"title": "Lead Coach Athletics", "description": "NTU | Jobs | Search here for your perfect career - Job Information  | Apply for Lead Coach Athletics Cookie Policy By clicking \"Allow Cookies\", you agree to the storing of cookies on your device to analyse site usage, and assist in our marketing efforts. Cookie Policy (Opens in a new tab) Decline Allow cookies Skip to main content List Vacancies (current) Sign in Accessibility Tools List Vacancies (current) Back to Search Results Lead Coach Athletics Apply for job Job reference: 552513 Location: Clifton Campus Employment type: Hourly Paid/Casual Contract Team: NTU Sport Closing date: 26/10/2026 School / Directorate: z.University Sports Activities Salary / Grade See special conditions Where to find us location_on Get directions Be part of something bigger. Doing things differently. NTU Sport are committed to having 70% of students engaged in sport and physical activity by 2025. Join us on our mission. Lead Athletics Coach \u00a320 per hour Zero Hours About the Role Are you passionate about athletics and helping athletes reach their potential? We're looking for a Lead Athletics Coach to lead and shape the coaching programme for Nottingham Trent University Athletics Club. In this role, you'll plan and deliver engaging training sessions for a diverse group of student-athletes, ranging from recreational participants to performance-level competitors. You'll work closely with club committee members, assistant coaches and NTU Sport staff to create a positive, inclusive and ambitious environment where students can thrive both on and off the track. You'll lead the development of training programmes, support athlete progression and help students balance their sporting commitments alongside university life. You'll also play an important role in supporting assistant coaches and volunteers to deliver an outstanding student experience. We're looking for someone with strong coaching experience, excellent communication skills and a passion for developing people. You'll be confident planning and leading sessions, providing constructive feedback and adapting your coaching approach to meet the needs of a wide range of athletes. Training takes place at Harvey Hadden Sports Village on Tuesday and Thursday evenings during term time. The successful candidate will therefore need to be able to travel to and from the venue on a regular basis. Access to a car may be beneficial but is not essential. Whether you're an experienced university coach or looking to take the next step in your coaching career, we'd love to hear from you Interviews Date: w/c 9th November 2026 About Us At NTU, we believe that sport is for everyone. That's why we are passionate about creating a welcoming and inclusive environment where our students, staff and the people of Nottingham feel inspired, supported and part of a community. Our core values are Pride, Unity and Respect, and these three pillars are embedded into everything we do at NTU Sport. From the way we deliver coaching and sports science support, to the way we design our world\u2013class facilities, we are committed to developing a culture of inclusivity and respect. Our determination to provide an outstanding service helped NTU secure 8th place in the British Universities & Colleges Sports (BUCS) championship 2022-23, cementing NTU as a top 10 university for Sport. Our Facilities We have a fantastic range of sports facilities at our City campuses, including industry-standard gym equipment, a 10m climbing wall, a sports hall, dance studios and a sports therapy suite offering physiotherapy and sports massage. Our Clifton campus is home to the Lee Westwood Sports Centre, a fully floodlit all-weather astro-turf pitch, three brand new squash courts, an exercise studio, sports hall, grass pitches and a newly refurbished fitness suite. Our Equestrian Centre at Brackenhurst features both indoor and outdoor arenas and holds a variety of events throughout the year, including unaffiliated and affiliated dressage competitions, and unaffiliated show jumping. For any informal queries about the role or the team, please contact Steven Drake Club Management Coordinator at steven.drake@ntu.ac.uk. Join Us We\u2019ll look after you with ongoing support, good development opportunities and a competitive salary that rewards your contribution. We also offer generous holidays, flexible working options, a pension scheme, great facilities and wide range of savings, discounts and benefits. Find out more about the range of benefits we offer. We are committed to advancing Equality, Diversity and Inclusion across all areas of our work. We actively promote a culture of respect and belonging and we welcome applications from people of all backgrounds. For more information please click here - Equality, Diversity and Inclusion | Nottingham Trent University Start to think about your future differently. Apply here. Safe and Inclusive At NTU, we continue to build an inclusive culture that encourages, supports and celebrates the diverse voices and experiences of our students and colleagues. By championing positive wellbeing, we promote an environment where all can thrive and reach their full potential. We welcome the unique contributions that you can bring and we encourage people from underrepresented communities and backgrounds to apply to join our team. Please note that unfortunately, this role has been assessed as ineligible for sponsorship under the UK Visas & Immigration points-based immigration system however, we recommend that you assess your eligibility before applying for this position. For more information visit the Government Skilled Worker visa support page. However, applications are welcome from candidates who do not currently have the right to work in the UK, but who would be eligible to obtain a valid visa via another route. Please consult the Home Office website for further information. Please note that this role is covered by the Rehabilitation of Offenders Act (1974) and successful applicants will be asked to declare any unspent criminal convictions. Supporting Documents save_alt JDPS- Lead Coach Athletics (PDF, KB) Take a look around the company https://www.ntu.ac.uk/ Apply for job favorite_border Save this job Go to main site Terms & Conditions Accessibility Nottingham Trent University\u00a0applicant tracking system delivered and supported by Jobtrain"}, "https://vacancies.ntu.ac.uk/Job/JobDetail?JobId=2508": {"title": "Network Coordinator", "description": "NTU | Jobs | Search here for your perfect career - Job Information  | Apply for Network Coordinator Skip to main content List Vacancies (current) Sign in Accessibility Tools List Vacancies (current) Back to Search Results Network Coordinator Apply for job Job reference: 552475 Location: Clifton Campus Employment type: Fixed Term Contract Team: Computer Science Closing date: 19/10/2026 School / Directorate: School of Science and Technology Salary / Grade Grade G (\u00a333,739 - \u00a338,825 p.a. pro rata) Where to find us location_on Get directions Be part of something bigger. Doing things differently. Network Coordinator- EPSRC Tiny UK Network Salary \u00a333,739 - \u00a338,825 per annum Full time/ Fixed term contract for 12 months Important Information: This is an in-person post based in Nottingham. It involves collaboration with other EPSRC-funded networks and international partners. The role requires regular travel across the UK and abroad to support workshops, co-creation activities, tutorials, Hackathons and national level events. About TinyML UK TinyML UK is a new national network funded by UKRI through EPSRC. It connects researchers, industry, engineers, AI specialists and government organisations working on decentralised, energy-efficient machine learning for small and low-power devices. The Network supports collaboration, training, events and real-world impact across health, sustainability and security, while contributing to a UK roadmap for TinyML research and skills. The Network is led by Professor Eiman Kanjo at Nottingham Trent University, with co-leads Professor Geoff Merrett at the University of Southampton and Professor Pantelis Georgiou at Imperial College London. Role overview We are seeking a proactive and service-focused Network Coordinator to provide reliable operational, administrative and project support to the Network Lead and leadership team. The postholder will help deliver agreed priorities and activities, using initiative to complete assigned work, identify issues and propose improvements within the Network\u2019s strategic direction. Key responsibilities Coordinate the Network\u2019s day-to-day administration and operations. Support large and small events, workshops, training, competitions, meetings and outreach activities. The opportunity to lead activities. Maintain project plans, records, reports, budgets and stakeholder communications. Liaise with academic, industry, government and international partners. Support funding bids, partnerships, laboratories and related academic or institutional initiatives. Provide responsive support to the Network Lead, leadership team and wider consortium. Learn new skills and use AI and digital tools to improve project delivery. Undertake other reasonable duties consistent with the role\u2019s purpose and grade as priorities develop. This is a full-time, 12-month fixed-term post, with the possibility of extension subject to continued funding, performance and operational requirements. Regular workplace attendance and occasional UK or international travel may be required. Further information is available at : https://tinyML.uk Please refer to the attached job description and person specification for full details. Interview date: TBC About Us The School of Science and Technology at Nottingham Trent University (NTU) is an exciting multidisciplinary environment for learning, teaching and research, with some of the best facilities in the UK. We pride ourselves on delivering high-quality teaching and diverse, real-world research. We specialise in biosciences, chemistry, computing and technology, as well as engineering, forensic science, mathematics, physics and sport science. This mix of traditional and modern subjects encourages and inspires future innovators. Our Department of Computer Science combines internationally-significant research with an outstanding record for teaching excellence. Our state-of-the-art facilities and career-focused approach to course design provide the right conditions for students to excel in their chosen fields. For any informal queries about the role or the team, please contact Prof. Eiman Kanjo Head of Smart Sensing Lab at eiman.kanjo@ntu.ac.uk Join Us Hybrid working - We support flexible ways of working through a combination of campus-based and home working where applicable. For full-time roles, this includes a minimum of 60% on-campus commitment. We trust colleagues to work with their teams to shape working patterns that enable them to deliver the best possible outcomes for their stakeholders. Flexibility - We welcome and support a range of working patterns and approaches, helping colleagues balance their work and personal commitments while meeting the needs of the role. 28 - 30 days annual leave, plus statutory bank holidays and 5 university closure days pro rata. Salary Sacrifice Retirement Savings Plan with life assurance and income protection. Available to colleagues who choose to opt out of the contractual pension scheme. Minimum colleague contributions of 0% matched with minimum NTU contributions of 8%. Range of health and wellbeing services, including a Health Cash Plan, voluntary benefits, discounts, and savings for all colleagues. Access to a wealth of formal and informal professional development opportunities to develop your skills and advance your career. We are committed to advancing Equality, Diversity and Inclusion across all areas of our work. We actively promote a culture of respect and belonging and we welcome applications from people of all backgrounds. For more information please click here - Equality, Diversity and Inclusion | Nottingham Trent University And a whole lot more\u2026Find out more about the range of benefits we offer. Come and be part of our success. Apply today. Safe and Inclusive At NTU, we continue to build an inclusive culture that encourages, supports and celebrates the diverse voices and experiences of our students and colleagues. By championing positive wellbeing, we promote an environment where all can thrive and reach their full potential. We welcome the unique contributions that you can bring and we encourage people from underrepresented communities and backgrounds to apply to join our team. Please note that unfortunately, this role has been assessed as ineligible for sponsorship under the UK Visas & Immigration points-based immigration system however, we recommend that you assess your eligibility before applying for this position. For more information visit the Government Skilled Worker visa support page. However, applications are welcome from candidates who do not currently have the right to work in the UK, but who would be eligible to obtain a valid visa via another route. Please consult the Home Office website for further information. Please note that this role is covered by the Rehabilitation of Offenders Act (1974) and successful applicants will be asked to declare any unspent criminal convictions. Take a look around the company https://www.ntu.ac.uk/ Apply for job favorite_border Save this job Go to main site Terms & Conditions Accessibility Nottingham Trent University\u00a0applicant tracking system delivered and supported by Jobtrain"}, "https://vacancies.ntu.ac.uk/Job/JobDetail?JobId=2570": {"title": "Lecturer/ Senior Lecturer in Law", "description": "NTU | Jobs | Search here for your perfect career - Job Information  | Apply for Lecturer/ Senior Lecturer in Law Skip to main content List Vacancies (current) Sign in Accessibility Tools List Vacancies (current) Back to Search Results Lecturer/ Senior Lecturer in Law Apply for job Job reference: 552536 Location: City Campus Employment type: Permanent Contract Team: Vocational and Professional Programmes Closing date: 18/10/2026 School / Directorate: Nottingham Law School Salary / Grade HE Lecturer or Senior Lecturer (\u00a339,984 - \u00a358,624 pa pro rata) Where to find us location_on Get directions Shape the Legal Minds of Tomorrow. Doing things differently. Lecturer or Senior Lecturer in Law Salary- Lecturer \u00a339,984-\u00a343,671 per annum Salary- Senior Lecturer \u00a346,320-\u00a358,624 per annum Full time/Permanent About the Role We welcome applications from across all areas of Law, with particular interest in candidates specialising in Criminal Law and Land/ Property Law. You must have recent teaching experience in Higher Education, as well as submitted your PhD or hold a professional qualification as any of the following: a solicitor or barrister a chartered legal executive (FCILEX) a trade mark attorney or a patent attorney in the jurisdiction of England and Wales If you are in the early stages of an academic career and are considering joining NTU, then our Early Career Academic Development Programme could be just right for you. If you are considering joining NTU as a Senior Lecturer you will benefit from our Senior Lecturer Career Framework , which recognises and rewards you based on your performance, contribution and achievement, and offers the opportunity of faster salary progression compared to the industry\u202faverage. Interview date: 29th October 2026 About Us Nottingham Law School (NLS) is one of the leading providers of academic and professional legal education in the country, with an established record of delivering innovative and transformational courses. We are one of the largest law schools in the UK, offering a range of undergraduate degrees, academic and practitioner taught postgraduate courses and a strong research degrees programme. In addition, our students can gain practical experience volunteering at NLS Legal, our multi-award-winning-teaching law firm, the only on-campus law firm at a UK Law School. Our School has built a reputation for excellence in the provision of legal education and in shaping the careers of solicitors, barristers and legal practitioners at both national and international levels. In addition to our outstanding research expertise, we have long established links with policy makers, professional bodies and leading law firms, including a growing number of significant international associations. We have an extensive record of delivering excellent bespoke training programmes for practitioners and professional bodies, and have strengths in commissioned research, both in the UK and overseas. For any informal queries about the role or the team, please contact Elyse Wakelin at elyse.wakelin02@ntu.ac.uk or Alexandra Kastrinou at alexandra.kastrinou@ntu.ac.uk Join Us Find out more about our academic community at NTU, including the support we offer to academics at all stages of their careers. We also offer: 30 - 35 days annual leave per year plus statutory bank holidays and 5 university closure days pro rata Salary Sacrifice Retirement Savings Plan with life assurance and income protection. Available to colleagues who choose to opt out of the contractual pension scheme. Minimum colleague contributions of 0% matched with minimum NTU contributions of 8%. Opportunity to receive a bonus for exceptional performance and contribution Range of health and wellbeing services, including a Health Cash Plan, voluntary benefits, discounts, and savings for all colleagues. We are committed to advancing Equality, Diversity and Inclusion across all areas of our work. We actively promote a culture of respect and belonging and we welcome applications from people of all backgrounds. For more information please click here - Equality, Diversity and Inclusion | Nottingham Trent University And a whole lot more\u2026Find out more about the range of benefits we offer. Come and be part of our success. Apply today. Safe and Inclusive At NTU, we continue to build an inclusive culture that encourages, supports and celebrates the diverse voices and experiences of our students and colleagues. By championing positive wellbeing, we promote an environment where all can thrive and reach their full potential. We welcome the unique contributions that you can bring and we encourage people from underrepresented communities and backgrounds to apply to join our team. Depending on your individual circumstances this role may be eligible for sponsorship under the UKVI Skilled Worker route. We recommend that you review your individual circumstances before applying, or for more information visit the Government Skilled Worker visa support page. This role is covered by the Rehabilitation of Offenders Act (1974) and successful applicants will be asked to declare any unspent criminal convictions. Take a look around the company https://www.ntu.ac.uk/ Apply for job favorite_border Save this job Go to main site Terms & Conditions Accessibility Nottingham Trent University\u00a0applicant tracking system delivered and supported by Jobtrain"}, "https://vacancies.ntu.ac.uk/Job/JobDetail?JobId=2576": {"title": "Social Media Officer", "description": "NTU | Jobs | Search here for your perfect career - Job Information  | Apply for Social Media Officer Cookie Policy By clicking \"Allow Cookies\", you agree to the storing of cookies on your device to analyse site usage, and assist in our marketing efforts. Cookie Policy (Opens in a new tab) Decline Allow cookies Skip to main content List Vacancies (current) Sign in Accessibility Tools List Vacancies (current) Back to Search Results Social Media Officer Apply for job Job reference: 552542 Location: City Campus Employment type: Permanent Contract Team: Brand and Content Closing date: 26/10/2026 School / Directorate: Communications, Alumni Relations, Marketing and Student Recruitment Salary / Grade Grade G (\u00a333,739 - \u00a338,825 p.a. pro rata) Where to find us location_on Get directions Be part of something bigger. Doing things differently. Social Media Officer Grade G (\u00a333,739 - \u00a338,825 p.a. pro rata) Full Time/Permanent About the Role We are looking for an experienced, driven and talented social media professional to join our Communications, Alumni Relations, Marketing and Student Recruitment (CAMS) department. The postholder will plan, deliver and implement social media content and campaigns to enhance NTU\u2019s global reputation and support the university\u2019s strategic priorities and objectives. Reporting to the Social Media Manager, the postholder will work collaboratively with teams across CAMS including the Marketing and Campaigns team, School Marketing teams and International Student Recruitment team, producing innovative and engaging content for NTU\u2019s organic social media channels (UK and international). With demonstrable content production and project management skills, you will have a strong track record of creating and editing engaging social media content for specific audiences and experience delivering multi-channel social media campaigns. You\u2019ll be a creative thinker with a keen eye for detail and possess excellent communication and stakeholder management skills along with the ability to manage competing deadlines and priorities. For more details, please take a look at the role profile. We'll still consider applications even if you don't meet every single one of the requirements, so don't be put off if you don't match them perfectly. About Us Our award-winning Department of Communications, Alumni Relations, Marketing and Student Recruitment (CAMS) is responsible for engaging with key audiences including prospective students to support NTU\u2019s student recruitment targets and driving forward NTU\u2019s reputation and brand. CAMS comprises admissions, applicant engagement, student recruitment events and outreach, international student recruitment, marketing and campaigns, content management, creative services, social media, web and digital, public relations and internal and external communications. If you have a passion for student recruitment, marketing and communications and a drive to make a real difference, CAMS at NTU could be the perfect place for you. In return, we offer you a culture of positivity, encouragement and mutual support. The senior leadership team are committed to nurturing talent and helping people reach their full potential. But most of all, we believe in change and growth; in daring to do things differently. For any informal queries about the role or the team, please contact Katy Law, Social Media Manager, at katy.law@ntu.ac.uk Interview date: 19 November 2026 Join Us Hybrid working - We support flexible ways of working through a combination of campus-based and home working where applicable. For full-time roles, this includes a minimum of 60% on-campus commitment. We trust colleagues to work with their teams to shape working patterns that enable them to deliver the best possible outcomes for their stakeholders. Flexibility - We welcome and support a range of working patterns and approaches, helping colleagues balance their work and personal commitments while meeting the needs of the role. 28 - 30 days annual leave, plus statutory bank holidays and 5 university closure days pro rata. Salary Sacrifice Retirement Savings Plan with life assurance and income protection. Available to colleagues who choose to opt out of the contractual pension scheme. Minimum colleague contributions of 0% matched with minimum NTU contributions of 8%. Range of health and wellbeing services, including a Health Cash Plan, voluntary benefits, discounts, and savings for all colleagues. Access to a wealth of formal and informal professional development opportunities to develop your skills and advance your career. We are committed to advancing Equality, Diversity and Inclusion across all areas of our work. We actively promote a culture of respect and belonging and we welcome applications from people of all backgrounds. For more information please click here - Equality, Diversity and Inclusion | Nottingham Trent University And a whole lot more\u2026Find out more about the range of benefits we offer. Come and be part of our success. Apply today. Safe and Inclusive At NTU, we continue to build an inclusive culture that encourages, supports and celebrates the diverse voices and experiences of our students and colleagues. By championing positive wellbeing, we promote an environment where all can thrive and reach their full potential. We welcome the unique contributions that you can bring and we encourage people from underrepresented communities and backgrounds to apply to join our team. Please note that unfortunately, this role has been assessed as ineligible for sponsorship under the UK Visas & Immigration points-based immigration system however, we recommend that you assess your eligibility before applying for this position. For more information visit the Government Skilled Worker visa support page. However, applications are welcome from candidates who do not currently have the right to work in the UK, but who would be eligible to obtain a valid visa via another route. Please consult the Home Office website for further information. Please note that this role is covered by the Rehabilitation of Offenders Act (1974) and successful applicants will be asked to declare any unspent criminal convictions. Supporting Documents save_alt 552542 - Social Media Officer JDPS (PDF, KB) Take a look around the company https://www.ntu.ac.uk/ Apply for job favorite_border Save this job Go to main site Terms & Conditions Accessibility Nottingham Trent University\u00a0applicant tracking system delivered and supported by Jobtrain"}, "https://vacancies.ntu.ac.uk/Job/JobDetail?JobId=2562": {"title": "Lead Coach - Netball", "description": "NTU | Jobs | Search here for your perfect career - Job Information  | Apply for Lead Coach - Netball Cookie Policy By clicking \"Allow Cookies\", you agree to the storing of cookies on your device to analyse site usage, and assist in our marketing efforts. Cookie Policy (Opens in a new tab) Decline Allow cookies Skip to main content List Vacancies (current) Sign in Accessibility Tools List Vacancies (current) Back to Search Results Lead Coach - Netball Apply for job Job reference: 552528 Location: Clifton Campus Employment type: Hourly Paid/Casual Contract Team: NTU Sport Closing date: 31/10/2026 School / Directorate: z.University Sports Activities Salary / Grade See special conditions (Shift work) Where to find us location_on Get directions Be part of something bigger. Doing things differently. NTU Sport are committed to having 70% of students engaged in sport and physical activity by 2025. Join us on our mission. Lead Coach - Netball Role is paid at \u00a320 per hour Games take place on Wednesday afternoons/ evenings Training is on a Monday evening Please note that delivery will primarily take place during term time About the Role This role will form part of the coaching delivery team for the BUCS Netball program at Nottingham Trent University, one of the top 10 ranked university Netball programs in the country. The role being recruited to will primarily focus on leading on the delivery of all training and matchday provision for our Netball BUCS (2s - 6s) who play in range of Tiers across BUCS. Additionally, you will be instrumental in the selection and retention of talented student athletes, both from within the UK and internationally, along with continuing to develop the thriving and successful performance culture at the heart of the club. With a strong history of delivering coaching to high quality players, you will be instrumental in ensuring that Nottingham Trent University continues to be one of the premier institutions for any student wanting to combine high level Netball with a high quality education. For more details, please take a look at the role profile. We'll still consider applications even if you don't meet every single one of the requirements, so don't be put off if you don't match them perfectly. Proposed interview date: TBC About Us At NTU, we believe that sport is for everyone. That's why we are passionate about creating a welcoming and inclusive environment where our students, staff and the people of Nottingham feel inspired, supported and part of a community. Our core values are Pride, Unity and Respect, and these three pillars are embedded into everything we do at NTU Sport. From the way we deliver coaching and sports science support, to the way we design our world\u2013class facilities, we are committed to developing a culture of inclusivity and respect. Our determination to provide an outstanding service has helped NTU secure multiple BUCS Top 10 finishes across the past decade Our Facilities We have a fantastic range of sports facilities at our City campuses, including industry-standard gym equipment, a 10m climbing wall, a sports hall, dance studios and a sports therapy suite offering physiotherapy and sports massage. Our Clifton campus is home to the Clifton Sports Hub, a fully floodlit 3G Pitch and state of the art all-weather hockey pitch, four grass pitches, three squash courts, an exercise studio, 2 sports halls, and four court tennis centre. For any informal queries about the role or the team, please contact Louise Hopkin (Head of Netball) at louise.hopkin@ntu.ac.uk. Join Us We\u2019ll look after you with ongoing support, good development opportunities and a competitive salary that rewards your contribution. We also offer generous holidays, flexible working options, a pension scheme, great facilities and wide range of savings, discounts and benefits. Find out more about the range of benefits we offer. Start to think about your future differently. Apply here. Safe and Inclusive At NTU, we continue to build an inclusive culture that encourages, supports and celebrates the diverse voices and experiences of our students and colleagues. We welcome the unique contributions that you can bring and we encourage people from underrepresented communities and backgrounds to apply to join our team. Please note that unfortunately, this role has been assessed as ineligible for sponsorship under the UK Visas & Immigration points-based immigration system. However, applications are welcome from candidates who do not currently have the right to work in the UK, but who would be eligible to obtain a valid visa via another route. Please consult the Home Office website for further information. Please note that this role is covered by the Rehabilitation of Offenders Act (1974) and successful applicants will be asked to declare any unspent criminal convictions. Work in the UK - GOV.UK Skilled Worker visa, Graduate visa, other work visas, right to work Supporting Documents save_alt 552528 - Lead Coach - Netball JDPS (PDF, KB) Take a look around the company https://www.ntu.ac.uk/ Apply for job favorite_border Save this job Go to main site Terms & Conditions Accessibility Nottingham Trent University\u00a0applicant tracking system delivered and supported by Jobtrain"}, "https://vacancies.ntu.ac.uk/Job/JobDetail?JobId=2388": {"title": "Lecturer in Event Production", "description": "NTU | Jobs | Search here for your perfect career - Job Information  | Apply for Lecturer in Event Production - Lighting (Teaching) Skip to main content List Vacancies (current) Sign in Accessibility Tools List Vacancies (current) Back to Search Results Lecturer in Event Production - Lighting (Teaching) Apply for job Job reference: 552356 Location: City Campus Employment type: Permanent Contract Team: ART School Office Closing date: 08/11/2026 School / Directorate: Nottingham School of Art & Design Salary / Grade HE Lecturer \u2013 TFL (\u00a339,984 - \u00a346,320 p.a. pro rata) Where to find us location_on Get directions Build a Rewarding Career. Doing things differently. Lecturer in Event Production - Lighting (Teaching) \u00a339,984 - \u00a343,671 per annum (pro rata) Permanent/Part time- 29.6 hours per week About the Role The core purpose of a Teaching-Focused Lecturer is to make a significant contribution to student success through the delivery of high-quality teaching and learning activities within the school. As a key member of the course team, you will contribute to the delivery of modules and course content, helping to ensure students receive an engaging, inclusive and supportive learning experience. You will also support a range of departmental activities, including student recruitment events, departmental meetings and the provision of pastoral support to students. Working closely with course leadership teams, you will help organise teaching resources effectively and play an active role in implementing enhancements to curriculum design and maintaining the school\u2019s high academic standards and excellent student experience and outcomes. You will bring strong subject knowledge, excellent written and verbal communication skills, and confidence in using a range of digital technologies to support learning and teaching. You will be comfortable working both independently and collaboratively and will contribute positively to teaching-related activities across the school. Above all, you will be passionate about supporting students to achieve their potential and succeed in their studies. Lecturer The Lecturer role provides a supportive framework for development and is suitable for a wide range of candidates, including recent graduates and those with limited teaching experience. For candidates who are new to higher education, the focus will be on developing confidence and capability in the delivery of learning and teaching activities, while contributing to the wider student experience and academic community. You will hold a degree in a relevant subject area or possess equivalent professional experience and/or teaching qualifications. For further information, please refer to the attached role profile. We welcome applications from candidates whose experience may not align with every requirement listed. If you are excited by the opportunity and believe you could make a positive contribution, we encourage you to apply. Interview date: W/C 21st September About Us Our Music & Events Department sits at the centre of a vibrant creative community, delivering industry-focused education across performance, production, sound, and live experiences. We prepare the next generation of creative professionals by combining artistic practice, technical expertise and real-world application. Based at our Metronome estate, in the heart of one of the UK\u2019s most dynamic creative cities, students benefit from access to state-of-the-art facilities, including: Professional recording studios and control rooms A large-scale live performance venue and black box space Specialist music and audio production and post-production studios Dedicated rehearsal rooms Live event production and technical facilities, supporting lighting, sound and staging These facilities are designed to replicate professional environments and support experiential learning, ensuring students graduate with the practical skills and confidence to succeed in the music and events industries. Our department brings together musicians, producers, costume and theatre designers, engineers and event professionals in a collaborative and forward-thinking environment. We place a strong emphasis on industry engagement, live briefs and applied learning, working closely with partners across the creative sector to ensure our courses remain relevant, innovative and impactful. For any informal queries about the role or the team, please contact John Meredith (Head of Department - Music and Events) at John.Meredith@ntu.ac.uk Join Us Find out more about our academic community at NTU, including the support we offer to academics at all stages of their careers. We also offer: 30 - 35 days annual leave per year plus statutory bank holidays and 5 university closure days pro rata Salary Sacrifice Retirement Savings Plan with life assurance and income protection. Available to colleagues who choose to opt out of the contractual pension scheme. Minimum colleague contributions of 0% matched with minimum NTU contributions of 8%. Opportunity to receive a bonus for exceptional performance and contribution Range of health and wellbeing services, including a Health Cash Plan, voluntary benefits, discounts, and savings for all colleagues. And a whole lot more\u2026Find out more about the range of benefits we offer. Come and be part of our success. Apply today. Safe and Inclusive At NTU, we continue to build an inclusive culture that encourages, supports and celebrates the diverse voices and experiences of our students and colleagues. By championing positive wellbeing, we promote an environment where all can thrive and reach their full potential. We welcome the unique contributions that you can bring and we encourage people from underrepresented communities and backgrounds to apply to join our team. Please note that unfortunately, this role has been assessed as ineligible for sponsorship under the UK Visas & Immigration points-based immigration system however, we recommend that you assess your eligibility before applying for this position. For more information visit the Government Skilled Worker visa support page. However, applications are welcome from candidates who do not currently have the right to work in the UK, but who would be eligible to obtain a valid visa via another route. Please consult the Home Office website for further information. Please note that this role is covered by the Rehabilitation of Offenders Act (1974) and successful applicants will be asked to declare any unspent criminal convictions. Safeguarding Statement Nottingham Trent University is committed to safeguarding and promoting the welfare of young people and expects all colleagues to share this commitment. If you are successful, you will be required to undertake an enhanced application and a Disclosure and Barring Service (DBS) check. The post for which you are applying is exempt from Section 4(2) of the Rehabilitation of Offenders Act 1974 requiring any spent convictions to be declared. Any information you provide will be treated in confidence and only used when considering your suitability for the post. Before you apply we recommend you ensure you are able to supply the documentation listed on the DBS website Take a look around the company https://www.ntu.ac.uk/ Apply for job favorite_border Save this job Go to main site Terms & Conditions Accessibility Nottingham Trent University\u00a0applicant tracking system delivered and supported by Jobtrain"}, "https://vacancies.ntu.ac.uk/Job/JobDetail?JobId=2494": {"title": "Hourly Paid Lecturer in Computer Science", "description": "NTU | Jobs | Search here for your perfect career - Job Information  | Apply for Hourly Paid Lecturer in Computer Science Skip to main content List Vacancies (current) Sign in Accessibility Tools List Vacancies (current) Back to Search Results Hourly Paid Lecturer in Computer Science Apply for job Job reference: 552461 Location: Clifton Campus Employment type: Hourly Paid/Casual Contract Team: Computer Science Closing date: 30/11/2026 School / Directorate: School of Science and Technology Salary / Grade HPL1 (\u00a339,984- \u00a344,977 p.a. pro rata) Where to find us location_on Get directions Build a Rewarding Career. Doing things differently. Hourly Paid Lecturer in Computer Science \u00a350.75 per direct hour, this includes 2 or more of the following elements: teaching, preparation and marking of the scheduled programme of work. A flat rate of \u00a320.72 per direct teaching hour will be paid for completing one of the above elements of the schedule. The number of hours required and the days of the week may vary. About the Role You will join the thriving and innovative Departments in our School of Science and Technology which are responsible for teaching and research in a variety of disciplines at undergraduate and postgraduate levels. We are looking for well-rounded academics with experience in the above disciplines, with a positive attitude that wish to be part of a forward looking Department. We are looking for hourly paid lecturers to teach on a range of programmes at undergraduate and postgraduate levels. This vacancy may close at any time once sufficient applications have been received. Early submission of your application is encouraged. For more details, please take a look at the role description and person specification provided below. We'll still consider applications even if you don't meet every single one of the requirements, so don't be put off if you don't match them perfectly. Interview Date: TBC About Us The School of Science and Technology at Nottingham Trent University (NTU) is an exciting multidisciplinary environment for learning, teaching and research, with some of the best facilities in the UK. We pride ourselves on delivering high-quality teaching and diverse, real-world research. We specialise in biosciences, chemistry, computing and technology, as well as engineering, forensic science, mathematics, physics and sport science. This mix of traditional and modern subjects encourages and inspires future innovators. Our Department of Computer Science combines internationally-significant research with an outstanding record for teaching excellence. Our state-of-the-art facilities and career-focused approach to course design provide the right conditions for students to excel in their chosen fields. For any informal queries about the role or the team, please contact Professor Ahmad Lotfi (Head of Department of Computer Science) , via CMPMgtAdmin@ntu.ac.uk Join Us We can offer you a career with a difference, as together we shape futures, change lives and create the university of the future. Doing things differently, we empower our people to shape, create and innovate. Whether they\u2019re pushing the boundaries with award-winning research, transforming society through global collaborations or supporting and helping our students to achieve their potential. Join our friendly and diverse community of 4,000 professionals, academics and researchers, and you\u2019ll enjoy the support and ownership you need to perform at your best. A great place to work, we value, respect and care for all our colleagues, providing flexible and competitive rewards and genuine opportunities for career progression. So, take on an exciting new challenge with an ambitious university where progress never stops. Safe & Inclusive At NTU, we continue to build an inclusive culture that encourages, supports and celebrates the diverse voices and experiences of our students and colleagues. We welcome the unique contributions that you can bring and we encourage people from underrepresented communities and backgrounds to apply to join our team. Please note that unfortunately, this role has been assessed as ineligible for sponsorship under the UK Visas & Immigration points-based immigration system, upcoming immigration rules (4th April 2024) changes may impact on eligibility for sponsorship, we recommend that you assess your eligibility before applying for this position. Visit https://www.gov.uk/skilled-worker-visa for more information. However, applications are welcome from candidates who do not currently have the right to work in the UK, but who would be eligible to obtain a valid visa via another route. Please consult the Home Office website for further information. Please note that this role is covered by the Rehabilitation of Offenders Act (1974) and successful applicants will be asked to declare any unspent criminal convictions. Take a look around the company https://www.ntu.ac.uk/ Apply for job favorite_border Save this job Go to main site Terms & Conditions Accessibility Nottingham Trent University\u00a0applicant tracking system delivered and supported by Jobtrain"}, "https://vacancies.ntu.ac.uk/Job/JobDetail?JobId=2317": {"title": "Building Services Technician (HVAC)", "description": "NTU | Jobs | Search here for your perfect career - Job Information  | Apply for Building Services Technician (HVAC) Skip to main content List Vacancies (current) Sign in Accessibility Tools List Vacancies (current) Back to Search Results Building Services Technician (HVAC) Apply for job Job reference: 552285 Location: City Campus Employment type: Permanent Contract Team: Energy, Engineering and Maintenance Closing date: 30/10/2026 School / Directorate: Estates and Campus Services Salary / Grade Grade G (\u00a333,739 - \u00a338,825 p.a. pro rata) Where to find us location_on Get directions Build a Rewarding Career. Doing things differently. Building Services Technician (HVAC) Salary \u00a333,739 - \u00a338,825 per annum Full time, permanent contract About the Role As a Building Services Technician (HVAC) you will be part of the in-house Estates team that supports and enables the safe, compliant and efficient operation of the university estate. The role is varied and diverse, with day-to-day duties ranging from ensuring that our estate is safe and operational, through to supporting the delivery of key University events such as open days and graduation ceremonies. Typical duties will include: Ensuring the safe and efficient operation of all building mechanical, ventilation and plumbing systems through the management and delivery of preventative planned maintenance, statutory inspections, remedial works and the efficient operation of the systems. Managing specialist contractors, including their procurement, safe delivery of works and performance management. Preparation and evaluation of small works/remedial work tenders, making recommendations with regards to the appointment of contractors and the awarding of works in line with all relevant NTU procurement requirements. Ensuring contract documents and health and safety documents are correctly executed and in place before work commences on site. For more details, please take a look at the role profile. We'll still consider applications even if you don't meet every single one of the requirements, so don't be put off if you don't match them perfectly - we're focused on finding the right person for the role. In your supporting statement please clearly outline how you meet the essential and desirable criteria, including examples of past relevant experience. Interview Date: w/c 16th November 2026 About Us Over the past 15 years, we\u2019ve invested more than \u00a3450m across our five campuses in Nottingham and Nottinghamshire. Named \u2018Modern University of the Year 2023\u2019 by The Times and The Sunday Times, we know that our campuses and facilities are a key part of our success, which is why we\u2019re investing a further \u00a3250m across our sites over the next five years. As one of the most environmentally responsible universities in the world, we lead the sector by embedding sustainability into everything we do. As part of our Estates team, you\u2019ll help to guide and support this work by reducing our carbon impact and accelerating our progress to net zero by 2040. Our Estates Our City campus is home to stunning Grade II listed buildings, dynamic architecture and picturesque living walls and terraces. In 2021, our renovation of a former Wesleyan Chapel (University Hall) was recognised as the \u2018University Impact Initiative of the Year\u2019 by the Association for University Directors of Estates (AUDE). We continue to invest in sector leading projects with the construction of the Design and Digital Arts building which will open in 2024. Recent developments at our Clifton campus include a \u00a323m Medical Technology Innovation Facility (MTIF), \u00a315m Health and Allied Professions Centre and \u00a31.6m Smart Wireless Innovation Facility (SWIFT). Our Brackenhurst campus offers a veterinary nursing centre, climate-controlled greenhouses, and multiple state-of-the-art laboratories. The Lyth building was completed in 2020 at a cost of \u00a311.5m and offers a wide range of high-quality teaching and social spaces. Our Confetti campus offers access to professional TV, film and music studios, as well as specialist labs, computer suites, industry-standard tech and world class facilities for Esports. From 2023, Confetti will be launching a second site in Whitechapel London, complete with a multipurpose, live events venue. Located at Vision West Nottinghamshire College, our \u00a36.5m Mansfield Hub opened in 2020 and includes state-of-the-art training facilities for clinical practitioners, as well as a sport science laboratory, lecture theatres and flexible study spaces. For any informal queries about the role or the team, please contact Scott Brooks (Head of Engineering, Maintenance and Operations) at scott.brooks@ntu.ac.uk Join Us Hybrid working - We support flexible ways of working through a combination of campus-based and home working where applicable. For full-time roles, this includes a minimum of 60% on-campus commitment. We trust colleagues to work with their teams to shape working patterns that enable them to deliver the best possible outcomes for their stakeholders. Flexibility - We welcome and support a range of working patterns and approaches, helping colleagues balance their work and personal commitments while meeting the needs of the role. 28 - 30 days annual leave, plus statutory bank holidays and 5 university closure days pro rata. Salary Sacrifice Retirement Savings Plan with life assurance and income protection. Available to colleagues who choose to opt out of the contractual pension scheme. Minimum colleague contributions of 0% matched with minimum NTU contributions of 8%. Range of health and wellbeing services, including a Health Cash Plan, voluntary benefits, discounts, and savings for all colleagues. Access to a wealth of formal and informal professional development opportunities to develop your skills and advance your career. We are committed to advancing Equality, Diversity and Inclusion across all areas of our work. We actively promote a culture of respect and belonging and we welcome applications from people of all backgrounds. For more information please click here - Equality, Diversity and Inclusion | Nottingham Trent University And a whole lot more\u2026Find out more about the range of benefits we offer. Come and be part of our success. Apply today. Safe and Inclusive At NTU, we continue to build an inclusive culture that encourages, supports and celebrates the diverse voices and experiences of our students and colleagues. By championing positive wellbeing, we promote an environment where all can thrive and reach their full potential. We welcome the unique contributions that you can bring and we encourage people from underrepresented communities and backgrounds to apply to join our team. Please note that unfortunately, this role has been assessed as ineligible for sponsorship under the UK Visas & Immigration points-based immigration system however, we recommend that you assess your eligibility before applying for this position. For more information visit the Government Skilled Worker visa support page. However, applications are welcome from candidates who do not currently have the right to work in the UK, but who would be eligible to obtain a valid visa via another route. Please consult the Home Office website for further information. Please note that this role is covered by the Rehabilitation of Offenders Act (1974) and successful applicants will be asked to declare any unspent criminal convictions. Take a look around the company https://www.ntu.ac.uk/ Apply for job favorite_border Save this job Go to main site Terms & Conditions Accessibility Nottingham Trent University\u00a0applicant tracking system delivered and supported by Jobtrain"}, "https://vacancies.ntu.ac.uk/Job/JobDetail?JobId=2271": {"title": "Technician Bank Staff", "description": "NTU | Jobs | Search here for your perfect career - Job Information  | Apply for Technician Bank Staff \u2013 Bio-Model Manufacture Skip to main content List Vacancies (current) Sign in Accessibility Tools List Vacancies (current) Back to Search Results Technician Bank Staff \u2013 Bio-Model Manufacture Apply for job Job reference: 552239 Location: City Campus Employment type: Hourly Paid/Casual Contract Team: Fashion Closing date: 01/06/2027 School / Directorate: Nottingham School of Art & Design Salary / Grade Grade E (\u00a328,063 - \u00a330,185 p.a. pro rata) Where to find us location_on Get directions Build a Rewarding Career. Doing things differently. Technician Bank Staff - Bio Model Manufacture Salary- \u00a327,246 - \u00a328,608 per annum (pro rata) Hourly paid contract paid on a project-by-project basis About the Role We\u2019re looking for a proactive and skilled individual to join our technical team, supporting the small\u2011scale production of silicone\u2011based bio\u2011models for industry partners and commercial clients. This is an exciting opportunity to work in a growing commercial environment within the Anatomical Replication and Manufacturing department, helping us deliver high\u2011quality products while contributing to a positive, industry\u2011focused workplace. In this hands\u2011on role, you will produce moulds and tools, prepare silicone-based composites, and ensure all materials, equipment and workspaces meet the highest standards. You will take responsibility for tracking material usage, supporting stock procurement, and carrying out routine maintenance to keep the manufacturing area running smoothly. The ideal candidate will be an enthusiastic team player, able to collaborate effectively with colleagues while also working independently when required. You will build and maintain strong internal and external contacts, stay up to date with developments in the field, and ensure Health and Safety regulations are consistently met. If you are organised, practical, and keen to share your skills within an innovative and commercially driven environment, we\u2019d love to hear from you. Apply now and help us shape the future of bio\u2011model manufacturing. For more details, please take a look at the role profile. We'll still consider applications even if you don't meet every single one of the requirements, so don't be put off if you don't match them perfectly. Interview Date: w/c 13th July 2026 About Us Our department is pioneering new ways to support surgical training and improve patient outcomes by transforming how surgeons prepare for complex procedures. Traditionally, surgeons have relied on cadavers or real patients to develop their skills, with limited opportunities to practice outside clinical settings. Led by Senior Research Fellow Richard Arm, our team is revolutionising this process through advanced manufacturing and medical modelling. By converting patient scan data into highly realistic 3D\u2011printed organs that match the exact shape, size and tactile qualities of human tissue, we provide surgeons with an accurate, hands-on platform for rehearsal. These innovations enable clinicians to refine techniques, anticipate challenges, and approach intricate or life\u2011saving surgeries with greater confidence and reduced risk. Find out more: Biomodels: Anatomical Replication and Manufacturing | Nottingham Trent University For any informal queries about the role please contact Richard Arm at richard.arm@ntu.ac.uk Join Us Hybrid working - we encourage and offer a mixture of office working and working from home. You're empowered to define how you work best for the benefits of your stakeholders. Flexibility - take ownership over how you get your work done. We're open to different working patterns and approaches. 25 - 30 days annual leave, plus statutory bank holidays and 5 university closure days pro rata. Salary Sacrifice Retirement Savings Plan with life assurance and income protection. Available to colleagues who choose to opt out of the contractual pension scheme. Minimum colleague contributions of 0% matched with minimum NTU contributions of 8%. Range of health and wellbeing services, including a Health Cash Plan, voluntary benefits, discounts, and savings for all colleagues. Access to a wealth of formal and informal professional development opportunities to develop your skills and advance your career. And a whole lot more\u2026Find out more about the range of benefits we offer. Come and be part of our success. Apply today. Safe and Inclusive At NTU, we continue to build an inclusive culture that encourages, supports and celebrates the diverse voices and experiences of our students and colleagues. By championing positive wellbeing, we promote an environment where all can thrive and reach their full potential. We welcome the unique contributions that you can bring and we encourage people from underrepresented communities and backgrounds to apply to join our team. Please note that unfortunately, this role has been assessed as ineligible for sponsorship under the UK Visas & Immigration points-based immigration system however, we recommend that you assess your eligibility before applying for this position. For more information visit the Government Skilled Worker visa support page. However, applications are welcome from candidates who do not currently have the right to work in the UK, but who would be eligible to obtain a valid visa via another route. Please consult the Home Office website for further information. Please note that this role is covered by the Rehabilitation of Offenders Act (1974) and successful applicants will be asked to declare any unspent criminal convictions. Take a look around the company https://www.ntu.ac.uk/ Apply for job favorite_border Save this job Go to main site Terms & Conditions Accessibility Nottingham Trent University\u00a0applicant tracking system delivered and supported by Jobtrain"}, "https://vacancies.ntu.ac.uk/Job/JobDetail?JobId=1569": {"title": "Demonstrator in Engineering", "description": "NTU | Jobs | Search here for your perfect career - Job Information  | Apply for Demonstrator in Engineering Cookie Policy By clicking \"Allow Cookies\", you agree to the storing of cookies on your device to analyse site usage, and assist in our marketing efforts. Cookie Policy (Opens in a new tab) Decline Allow cookies Skip to main content List Vacancies (current) Sign in Accessibility Tools List Vacancies (current) Back to Search Results Demonstrator in Engineering Apply for job Job reference: 551538 Location: Clifton Campus Employment type: Hourly Paid/Casual Contract Team: Engineering Closing date: 04/01/2027 School / Directorate: School of Science and Technology Salary / Grade See special conditions Where to find us location_on Get directions Build a Rewarding Career. Doing things differently. Demonstrator in Engineering \u00a314.54 per direct teaching support The number of hours required and the days of the week may vary. About the Role We are seeking to recruit a Laboratory demonstrator, who will be available to work throughout the academic year and will be paid on an hourly basis (up to a maximum of 100 hours per annum). In the Department of Engineering, we provide our students opportunities to gain knowledge and skills through laboratory and seminar sessions in the Engineering Building (Clifton campus). The students are studying a mixture of mechanical, electronics, biomedical and sport subjects. In order to ensure that we provide an excellent student experience we support these sessions with the use of demonstrators who offer support and advice to the students throughout the sessions. You will work under the direction of a module leader and other academics leading the session in delivering high quality demonstrating to undergraduate and/or postgraduate students. Duties will include assisting the academic staff in running the class \u2013 offering advice and support to students, liaising with technical staff and marking where required. You must be able to demonstrate excellent interpersonal skills and have the ability to communicate ideas of a complex or technical nature to students effectively, as well as having sound engineering knowledge. Interview date \u2013 Ongoing as required Hourly paid Demonstrators are hired throughout the year by the Department of Engineering. Please submit your application to express interest in being added to our demonstrator list. However, your application will not be processed further unless a suitable opportunity arises. About Us The School of Science and Technology at Nottingham Trent University (NTU) is an exciting multidisciplinary environment for learning, teaching and research, with some of the best facilities in the UK. We pride ourselves on delivering high-quality teaching and diverse, real-world research. We specialise in biosciences, chemistry, computing and technology, as well as engineering, forensic science, mathematics, physics and sport science. This mix of traditional and modern subjects encourages and inspires future innovators. In the Department of Engineering we deliver research and teaching in electronic engineering, mechanical engineering, biomedical engineering and sport engineering. We are building a global reputation in areas including human performance and human factors, future materials, biomedical engineering, and robotics. We are working with industrial partners in technology, automotive, aircraft, marine, healthcare engineering, and with sports teams to help them beat world records. For any informal queries about the role or the team, please contact Dr Ben Simpson - ben.simpson@ntu.ac.uk Join Us We can offer you a career with a difference, as together we shape futures, change lives and create the university of the future. Doing things differently, we empower our people to shape, create and innovate. Whether they\u2019re pushing the boundaries with award-winning research, transforming society through global collaborations or supporting and helping our students to achieve their potential. Join our friendly and diverse community of 4,000 professionals, academics and researchers, and you\u2019ll enjoy the support and ownership you need to perform at your best. A great place to work, we value, respect and care for all our colleagues, providing flexible and competitive rewards and genuine opportunities for career progression. So, take on an exciting new challenge with an ambitious university where progress never stops. Safe and Inclusive At NTU, we continue to build an inclusive culture that encourages, supports and celebrates the diverse voices and experiences of our students and colleagues. We welcome the unique contributions that you can bring and we encourage people from underrepresented communities and backgrounds to apply to join our team. Please note that unfortunately, this role has been assessed as ineligible for sponsorship under the UK Visas & Immigration points-based immigration system however, we recommend that you assess your eligibility before applying for this position. Visit https://www.gov.uk/skilled-worker-visa for more information. However, applications are welcome from candidates who do not currently have the right to work in the UK, but who would be eligible to obtain a valid visa via another route. Please consult the Home Office website for further information. Please note that this role is covered by the Rehabilitation of Offenders Act (1974) and successful applicants will be asked to declare any unspent criminal convictions. Supporting Documents save_alt 551538 - Demonstrator Engineering JDPS (PDF, KB) Take a look around the company https://www.ntu.ac.uk/ Apply for job favorite_border Save this job Go to main site Terms & Conditions Accessibility Nottingham Trent University\u00a0applicant tracking system delivered and supported by Jobtrain"}, "https://vacancies.ntu.ac.uk/Job/JobDetail?JobId=181": {"title": "Short Course Tutor", "description": "NTU | Jobs | Search here for your perfect career - Job Information  | Apply for Short Course Tutor Cookie Policy By clicking \"Allow Cookies\", you agree to the storing of cookies on your device to analyse site usage, and assist in our marketing efforts. Cookie Policy (Opens in a new tab) Decline Allow cookies Skip to main content List Vacancies (current) Sign in Accessibility Tools List Vacancies (current) Back to Search Results Short Course Tutor Apply for job Job reference: 550150 Location: City Campus Employment type: Hourly Paid/Casual Contract Team: Not specified Closing date: 01/12/2026 School / Directorate: z.Knowledge Exchange Salary / Grade See special conditions Where to find us location_on Get directions Build a Rewarding Career. Doing things differently. Short Course Tutors Experienced tutors and creative professionals are invited to submit proposals for innovative new short courses that will complement our existing portfolio. We are especially interested in those with skills and knowledge in the following themes 3D Modelling and Animation AI Literacy in Creative Practice Creative Branding and Design Idea Generation and Productivity Data Analytics for Creative Businesses Project Management for Creative Professionals Sustainable Design UX and UI Human-Centred Design Video Production. In addition to the above, we also welcome proposals related to creating, making and digital skills in: Architecture and interior design Audience engagement and content creation Creative writing Digital screen arts Fashion, textiles and costume Film and television Fine art Game arts Graphic design and illustration Ideas and innovation Journalism, media, communications and PR Photography Product design. You can read about the courses at www.ntu.ac.uk/creativeshortcourses Short Courses are designed to equip professionals with industry-relevant skills and opportunities to engage directly with current practices and expert practitioners, whilst supporting continuing professional development (CPD) for those looking to upskill or pivot their careers, as well as welcoming enthusiastic learners seeking high-quality creative enrichment and experiences. We also offer a dedicated portfolio of courses tailored specifically for young people aged 15 \u2013 17 years old. To support our international groups, we are also interested to hear from qualified and experienced tutors of English as a Foreign Language. About the Role Short course tutors use their industry experience to help learners navigate specialist creative and digital subjects, providing them with opportunities to maximise their professional or academic development. With an awareness of resources and events in the East Midlands, you will manage and deliver your short course and make a positive impact on the careers of your attendees. You will be able to build rapport with them through an enthusiastic and confident approach to delivery. The courses are fee paying, so a focus on the customer experience and value for money is paramount. You'll receive a management fee for preparing and delivering your short course. This will be discussed and negotiated with the Short Course Manager. For more details, take a look at the role profile. We'll consider applications even if you don't meet every single one of the requirements. Next Steps If you have an idea for a short course, apply and submit your proposal as part of your application. You should refer to the guidance document below for support in writing your proposal. You will be required to explain in no more than 200 words the training course you wish to propose. You can put more than one proposal on one application. However, applications received with no proposal will not be considered. Include information on the content that will be covered in the course, who your audience will be and why someone would want to do this course, with a clear explanation of why the subject is relevant today. You can only attach two documents, so we encourage you to upload your proposal in the same document as the Cover Letter, as a Word or PDF document. This advert is part of a rolling recruitment campaign which means applications are reviewed regularly. If your course looks exciting, relevant and innovative, you\u2019ll be invited to meet with the short course team to discuss it in more detail. For informal enquiries please contact Aimee Bollu, Short Course Manager on +44 (0)115 848 2394 or by email at aimee.bollu@ntu.ac.uk. About our Courses We already run an impressive portfolio of short courses that take place during the daytimes, evenings and weekends. Our ambition is to be a widely acknowledged force for good in economic, social and cultural development. We offer a vibrant learning atmosphere that encourages creativity and experimentation in our short course attendees, whether they be professionals enhancing their CV or beginners taking their first steps. Safe and Inclusive At NTU, we continue to build an inclusive culture that encourages, supports and celebrates the diverse voices and experiences of our students and colleagues. We welcome the unique contributions that you can bring and we encourage people from underrepresented communities and backgrounds to apply to join our team. Please note that unfortunately, this role has been assessed as ineligible for sponsorship under the UK Visas & Immigration points-based immigration system. However, applications are welcome from candidates who do not currently have the right to work in the UK, but who would be eligible to obtain a valid visa via another route. Please consult the Home Office website for further information. Please note that this role is covered by the Rehabilitation of Offenders Act (1974) and successful applicants will be asked to declare any unspent criminal convictions. Please note that if your role includes teaching 15 \u2013 17 year olds and as we have cross campus roles available depending on your campus allocation, if successful you may be required to undertake an enhanced application process and a Disclosure and Barring Service (DBS) check. Any information you provide will be treated in confidence and only used when considering your suitability for the post. Supporting Documents save_alt Short Course Proposal Guidance (PDF, KB) save_alt Role Description - Short Course Tutor (PDF, KB) Take a look around the company https://www.ntu.ac.uk/ Apply for job favorite_border Save this job Go to main site Terms & Conditions Accessibility Nottingham Trent University\u00a0applicant tracking system delivered and supported by Jobtrain"}, "https://vacancies.ntu.ac.uk/Job/JobDetail?JobId=2675": {"title": "International Applicant Engagement and Administration Associate", "description": "NTU | Jobs | Search here for your perfect career - Job Information  | Apply for International Applicant Engagement and Administration Associate Skip to main content List Vacancies (current) Sign in Accessibility Tools List Vacancies (current) Back to Search Results International Applicant Engagement and Administration Associate Apply for job Job reference: 552640 Location: City Campus Employment type: Fixed Term Contract Team: International Student Recruitment Closing date: 01/11/2026 School / Directorate: Communications, Alumni Relations, Marketing and Student Recruitment Salary / Grade Grade E (\u00a328,063 - \u00a330,185 p.a. pro rata) Where to find us location_on Get directions Be part of something bigger. Doing things differently. International Applicant Engagement and Administration Associate Salary- \u00a328,063 - \u00a330,185 per annum 9 months Fixed Term Contract (January - September 2027) About the Role An exciting opportunity to join the International team, part of the Communications, Alumni Relations, Marketing and Student Recruitment (CAMS) department at NTU. You will support international students as they make a life changing decision to study in the UK. Working within an experienced team, who will provide training and development, you'll communicate with prospective students all over the world. If you love providing excellent customer service this job will be perfect for you. Using your communication skills through email, phone and other online channels you'll chat with future NTU students to support them as they apply to the university. You'll also work on administration tasks which require excellent attention to detail as you manage important customer information and data. The team has a track record of supporting colleagues to develop in their career - with many previous colleagues progressing from this role within the department. So this is a ideal opportunity if you are a motivated and customer orientated graduate ready to begin your career. For more details, please take a look at the role profile. We'll still consider applications even if you don't meet every single one of the requirements, so don't be put off if you don't match them perfectly. To ensure the diverse needs of our team are met we actively encourage secondments and offer flexible part-time working patterns - we're focused on finding the right person for the role. We welcome internal candidates for secondment opportunities Interview Date: w/c 23rd November 2026 About Us Our award-winning Department of Communications, Alumni Relations, Marketing and Student Recruitment (CAMS) is responsible for engaging with key audiences including prospective students to support NTU\u2019s student recruitment targets and driving forward NTU\u2019s reputation and brand. CAMS comprises admissions, applicant engagement, student recruitment events and outreach, international student recruitment, marketing and campaigns, content management, creative services, social media, web and digital, public relations and internal and external communications. If you have a passion for student recruitment, marketing and communications and a drive to make a real difference, CAMS at NTU could be the perfect place for you. In return, we offer you a culture of positivity, encouragement and mutual support. The senior leadership team are committed to nurturing talent and helping people reach their full potential. But most of all, we believe in change and growth; in daring to do things differently. For any informal queries about the role or the team, please contact Laura Coates (International Administration and Enquiries Officer) at laura.coates@ntu.ac.uk Join Us Hybrid working - We support flexible ways of working through a combination of campus-based and home working where applicable. For full-time roles, this includes a minimum of 60% on-campus commitment. We trust colleagues to work with their teams to shape working patterns that enable them to deliver the best possible outcomes for their stakeholders. Flexibility - We welcome and support a range of working patterns and approaches, helping colleagues balance their work and personal commitments while meeting the needs of the role. 28 - 30 days annual leave, plus statutory bank holidays and 5 university closure days pro rata. Salary Sacrifice Retirement Savings Plan with life assurance and income protection. Available to colleagues who choose to opt out of the contractual pension scheme. Minimum colleague contributions of 0% matched with minimum NTU contributions of 8%. Range of health and wellbeing services, including a Health Cash Plan, voluntary benefits, discounts, and savings for all colleagues. Access to a wealth of formal and informal professional development opportunities to develop your skills and advance your career. We are committed to advancing Equality, Diversity and Inclusion across all areas of our work. We actively promote a culture of respect and belonging and we welcome applications from people of all backgrounds. For more information please click here - Equality, Diversity and Inclusion | Nottingham Trent University And a whole lot more\u2026Find out more about the range of benefits we offer. Come and be part of our success. Apply today. Safe and Inclusive At NTU, we continue to build an inclusive culture that encourages, supports and celebrates the diverse voices and experiences of our students and colleagues. By championing positive wellbeing, we promote an environment where all can thrive and reach their full potential. We welcome the unique contributions that you can bring and we encourage people from underrepresented communities and backgrounds to apply to join our team. Please note that unfortunately, this role has been assessed as ineligible for sponsorship under the UK Visas & Immigration points-based immigration system however, we recommend that you assess your eligibility before applying for this position. For more information visit the Government Skilled Worker visa support page. However, applications are welcome from candidates who do not currently have the right to work in the UK, but who would be eligible to obtain a valid visa via another route. Please consult the Home Office website for further information. Please note that this role is covered by the Rehabilitation of Offenders Act (1974) and successful applicants will be asked to declare any unspent criminal convictions. Take a look around the company https://www.ntu.ac.uk/ Apply for job favorite_border Save this job Go to main site Terms & Conditions Accessibility Nottingham Trent University\u00a0applicant tracking system delivered and supported by Jobtrain"}, "https://vacancies.ntu.ac.uk/Job/JobDetail?JobId=2722": {"title": "Hourly Paid Lecturer", "description": "NTU | Jobs | Search here for your perfect career - Job Information  | Apply for Hourly Paid Lecturer - Accounting and Finance Skip to main content List Vacancies (current) Sign in Accessibility Tools List Vacancies (current) Back to Search Results Hourly Paid Lecturer - Accounting and Finance Apply for job Job reference: 552687 Location: City Campus Employment type: Hourly Paid/Casual Contract Team: Accounting and Finance Closing date: 03/11/2026 School / Directorate: Nottingham Business School Salary / Grade HPL1 (\u00a339,984- \u00a344,977 p.a. pro rata) Where to find us location_on Get directions Empower Future Leaders. Doing things differently. Hourly Paid Lecturer - Accounting and Finance \u00a350.75 per direct teaching hour. This includes 2 or more of the following elements: teaching, preparation and marking of the scheduled programme of work. A flat rate of \u00a320.72 per direct teaching hour will be paid for completing one of the above elements of the schedule. The number of hours required and the days of the week may vary. About the Role We are seeking to recruit hourly paid lecturers who are available to work during the academic year and will be paid on an hourly basis. You will be teaching and supporting undergraduates and postgraduate students across the range of courses. We are looking for people with expertise in any of the following areas: Financial and Management Accounting Corporate Finance and Financial Management Taxation Corporate Governance Risk Management For more details, please take a look at the role profile. We'll still consider applications even if you don't meet every single one of the requirements, so don't be put off if you don't match them perfectly. Interviews: 9th November 2026 For more details, please take a look at the role profile. We'll still consider applications even if you don't meet every single one of the requirements, so don't be put off if you don't match them perfectly. To ensure the diverse needs of our team are met we actively encourage secondments and offer flexible part-time working patterns - we're focused on finding the right person for the role. About Us Nottingham Business School (NBS) delivers research and education that combine academic excellence with real-world impact on people, business, and society. We lead in experiential learning and personalised education, and our research drives positive change across social and economic spheres. This informs all our programmes, from undergraduate to doctoral. With strong partnerships across business, public, and voluntary sectors, NBS is known as the business school for business . We hold the prestigious Triple Crown Accreditation (EQUIS, AACSB, AMBA), placing us in the top 1% of business schools worldwide. Discover more on our website . At NTU, we do things differently. Join one of Europe\u2019s largest and most innovative business schools to help shape inclusive research and make a real difference. For any informal queries about the role or the team, please contact please contact Vangelis Tsiligkiris (Head of Accounting and Finance Department) at vangelis.tsiligiris@ntu.ac.uk. Join Us Find out more about our academic community at NTU, including the support we offer to academics at all stages of their careers. We also offer: 30 - 35 days annual leave per year plus statutory bank holidays and 5 university closure days pro rata Salary Sacrifice Retirement Savings Plan with life assurance and income protection. Available to colleagues who choose to opt out of the contractual pension scheme. Minimum colleague contributions of 0% matched with minimum NTU contributions of 8%. Opportunity to receive a bonus for exceptional performance and contribution Range of health and wellbeing services, including a Health Cash Plan, voluntary benefits, discounts, and savings for all colleagues. And a whole lot more\u2026Find out more about the range of benefits we offer. Come and be part of our success. Apply today. Safe & Inclusive At NTU, we continue to build an inclusive culture that encourages, supports and celebrates the diverse voices and experiences of our students and colleagues. By championing positive wellbeing, we promote an environment where all can thrive and reach their full potential. We welcome the unique contributions that you can bring and we encourage people from underrepresented communities and backgrounds to apply to join our team. Please note that unfortunately, this role has been assessed as ineligible for sponsorship under the UK Visas & Immigration points-based immigration system however, we recommend that you assess your eligibility before applying for this position. For more information visit the Government Skilled Worker visa support page. However, applications are welcome from candidates who do not currently have the right to work in the UK, but who would be eligible to obtain a valid visa via another route. Please consult the Home Office website for further information. Please note that this role is covered by the Rehabilitation of Offenders Act (1974) and successful applicants will be asked to declare any unspent criminal convictions. Take a look around the company https://www.ntu.ac.uk/ Apply for job favorite_border Save this job Go to main site Terms & Conditions Accessibility Nottingham Trent University\u00a0applicant tracking system delivered and supported by Jobtrain"}, "https://vacancies.ntu.ac.uk/Job/JobDetail?JobId=2709": {"title": "Hourly Paid Lecturer in Applied Linguistics", "description": "NTU | Jobs | Search here for your perfect career - Job Information  | Apply for Hourly Paid Lecturer in Applied Linguistics Skip to main content List Vacancies (current) Sign in Accessibility Tools List Vacancies (current) Back to Search Results Hourly Paid Lecturer in Applied Linguistics Apply for job Job reference: 552674 Location: City Campus Employment type: Hourly Paid/Casual Contract Team: Nottingham Institute of Languages and Intercultural Communication Closing date: 18/10/2026 School / Directorate: School of Social Sciences Salary / Grade HPL1 (\u00a339,984- \u00a344,977 p.a. pro rata) Where to find us location_on Get directions Build a Rewarding Career. Doing things differently. Hourly Paid Lecturer - (Linguistics) \u00a350.75 per direct teaching hour. This includes 2 or more of the following elements: teaching, preparation and marking of the scheduled programme of work. A flat rate of \u00a320.72 per direct teaching hour will be paid for completing one of the above elements of the schedule. The number of hours required and the days of the week may vary. About the Role We are looking for a colleague who can contribute to the delivery of selected modules on our BA English Language and Linguistics and our MA TESOL. We are particularly interested in applicants with teaching and research expertise in corpus-based approaches and competence in the teaching of research methods (including quantitative and qualitative methods). For more details, please take a look at the role profile. We'll still consider applications even if you don't meet every single one of the requirements, so don't be put off if you don't match them perfectly. The School of Social Sciences at Nottingham Trent University (NTU) is recognised nationally and internationally for delivering theoretically informed and applied leanring, teaching, and research. We foster a culture that values the diversity of all our communities and publicises and celebrates excellence in all we do. The Nottingham Institute of Languages and Intercultural Communications is a diverse, supportive, and collaborative community in which to innovate, explore and create. Our specialities span across a range of subject areas, including Applied Linguistics, English language teaching, foreign language learning, Academic English, and Intercultural Communication. We maintain a vibrant and inclusive international learning and teaching environment that is grounded in scholarship, research, and professional practice. Our courses are built on the ethos of developing intellectual and practical skills, adding value to students\u2019 employability and providing an outstanding student experience. For any informal queries about the role or the team, please contact Associate Professor David Wright at david.wright @ntu.ac.uk . Take a look around the company https://www.ntu.ac.uk/ Apply for job favorite_border Save this job Go to main site Terms & Conditions Accessibility Nottingham Trent University\u00a0applicant tracking system delivered and supported by Jobtrain"}, "https://vacancies.ntu.ac.uk/Job/JobDetail?JobId=2691": {"title": "Lecturer / Senior Lecturer CSI", "description": "NTU | Jobs | Search here for your perfect career - Job Information  | Apply for Lecturer / Senior Lecturer CSI Skip to main content List Vacancies (current) Sign in Accessibility Tools List Vacancies (current) Back to Search Results Lecturer / Senior Lecturer CSI Apply for job Job reference: 552656 Location: Clifton Campus Employment type: Permanent Contract Team: Chemistry and Forensics Closing date: 05/11/2026 School / Directorate: School of Science and Technology Salary / Grade HE Lecturer or Senior Lecturer (\u00a339,984 - \u00a358,624 pa pro rata) Where to find us location_on Get directions Diverse community. Inclusive Research. Rewarding Careers. Doing things differently. Lecturer/Senior Lecturer Crime Scene Investigation HE Lecturer \u00a339,984 - \u00a343,671 per annum (pro rata) Part time (0.7 FTE) About the Role Join our ambitious and highly regarded Forensic Science team and help shape the next generation of crime scene investigators. Whether your experience comes from industry, academia, or a combination of both, you will play a key role in delivering an outstanding student experience across our accredited undergraduate and postgraduate programmes. In this role, you will: Teach and support students across a range of forensic science and crime scene investigation modules. Share your expertise in crime scene processing, crime scene management, and related professional practice. Design and deliver engaging learning experiences through laboratories, workshops, seminars, field activities, and research projects. Develop teaching materials and contribute to the continual enhancement of our curriculum. Assess student work, provide constructive feedback, and support student progression and success. Contribute to the management, quality assurance, and ongoing development of our forensic science courses. Undertake research, scholarly, pedagogic, or professional practice activities that enhance your subject expertise and inform teaching. Work collaboratively with colleagues to maintain the high standards expected of programmes accredited by the Chartered Society of Forensic Sciences. You will be part of a department committed to innovation, student success, and professional relevance. Our Forensic Science programmes are recognised among the UK's top five courses in the subject area, providing an exciting environment in which to develop your academic and professional career. If you are passionate about forensic science, enjoy inspiring students, and want to help develop future practitioners, we would love to hear from you. For more details, please take a look at the role profile. We'll still consider applications even if you don't meet every single one of the requirements, so don't be put off if you don't match them perfectly. To ensure the diverse needs of our team are met we actively encourage secondments and offer flexible part-time working patterns - we're focused on finding the right person for the role. About Us The School of Science and Technology at Nottingham Trent University (NTU) is an exciting multidisciplinary environment for learning, teaching and research, with some of the best facilities in the UK. We pride ourselves on delivering high-quality teaching and diverse, real-world research. We specialise in biosciences, chemistry, computing and technology, as well as engineering, forensic science, mathematics, physics and sport science. This mix of traditional and modern subjects encourages and inspires future innovators. Our industry-standard Forensic Science facilities and equipment support our teaching and research and they are also used regularly by external organisations. Our crime scene training facility is one of the largest in the UK and is regularly used for teaching, training and research. For any informal queries about the role or the team, please contact Rachel Bolton King (Courses Manager Forensic Science) at rachel.bolton-king@ntu.ac.uk. Join Us Find out more about our academic community at NTU, including the support we offer to academics at all stages of their careers. We also offer: Hybrid working - We support flexible ways of working through a combination of campus-based and home working where applicable. For full-time roles, this includes a minimum of 60% on-campus commitment. We trust colleagues to work with their teams to shape working patterns that enable them to deliver the best possible outcomes for their stakeholders. Flexibility - We welcome and support a range of working patterns and approaches, helping colleagues balance their work and personal commitments while meeting the needs of the role. 30 - 35 days annual leave per year plus statutory bank holidays and 5 university closure days pro rata Salary Sacrifice Retirement Savings Plan with life assurance and income protection. Available to colleagues who choose to opt out of the contractual pension scheme. Minimum colleague contributions of 0% matched with minimum NTU contributions of 8%. Opportunity to receive a bonus for exceptional performance and contribution Range of health and wellbeing services, including a Health Cash Plan, voluntary benefits, discounts, and savings for all colleagues. We are committed to advancing Equality, Diversity and Inclusion across all areas of our work. We actively promote a culture of respect and belonging and we welcome applications from people of all backgrounds. For more information please click here - Equality, Diversity and Inclusion | Nottingham Trent University And a whole lot more\u2026Find out more about the range of benefits we offer. Come and be part of our success. Apply today. Safe and Inclusive At NTU, we continue to build an inclusive culture that encourages, supports and celebrates the diverse voices and experiences of our students and colleagues. By championing positive wellbeing, we promote an environment where all can thrive and reach their full potential. We welcome the unique contributions that you can bring and we encourage people from underrepresented communities and backgrounds to apply to join our team. Please note that unfortunately, this role has been assessed as ineligible for sponsorship under the UK Visas & Immigration points-based immigration system however, we recommend that you assess your eligibility before applying for this position. For more information visit the Government Skilled Worker visa support page. However, applications are welcome from candidates who do not currently have the right to work in the UK, but who would be eligible to obtain a valid visa via another route. Please consult the Home Office website for further information. Please note that this role is covered by the Rehabilitation of Offenders Act (1974) and successful applicants will be asked to declare any unspent criminal convictions. Take a look around the company https://www.ntu.ac.uk/ Apply for job favorite_border Save this job Go to main site Terms & Conditions Accessibility Nottingham Trent University\u00a0applicant tracking system delivered and supported by Jobtrain"}, "https://vacancies.ntu.ac.uk/Job/JobDetail?JobId=430": {"title": "Senior Research Fellow", "description": "NTU | Jobs | Search here for your perfect career - Job Information  | Apply for Senior Research Fellow Skip to main content List Vacancies (current) Sign in Accessibility Tools List Vacancies (current) Back to Search Results Senior Research Fellow Apply for job Job reference: 550399 Location: City Campus Employment type: Fixed Term Contract Team: Masters and Legal Research Closing date: 31/10/2026 School / Directorate: Nottingham Law School Salary / Grade Grade I (\u00a349,127 - \u00a358,624 p.a. pro rata) Where to find us location_on Get directions Build a Rewarding Career. Doing things differently. Senior Research Fellow in Law Salary \u00a349,127 - \u00a358,624 per annum (pro rata) Part time- 7.4 hours per week/ Fixed term for 6 months About the Role Would you like your research to help improve how public inquiries work across the UK? As a Senior Research Fellow in Nottingham Law School, you will support the delivery of a programme of work designed to improve the effectiveness, impact and value of public inquiries and strengthen their contribution to learning, policy development and organisational change. Working closely with the project lead, you will contribute to research, stakeholder engagement and project delivery activities. You will monitor developments across public inquiries and identify procedural, operational and reporting issues relevant to the project. You will engage with inquiry chairs, secretaries, practitioners, policymakers, advocacy groups and other stakeholders, coordinate participation in interviews, focus groups and other project work, quality-assure materials, identify emerging themes, and contribute to the planning, coordination and delivery of the project. Throughout, you will exercise sound judgement, work collaboratively, and maintain high standards of confidentiality, research ethics and data protection. This is a 0.2 FTE role, equivalent to 7.4 hours per week. It offers an opportunity to contribute to a focused, policy-relevant programme of work and support practical resources that can promote learning and improvement across UK public inquiries. Interview w/c 16th October 2026 About Us Nottingham Law School (NLS) is one of the leading providers of academic and professional legal education in the country, with an established record of delivering innovative and transformational courses. We are one of the largest law schools in the UK, offering a range of undergraduate degrees, academic and practitioner taught postgraduate courses and a strong research degrees programme. In addition, our students can gain practical experience volunteering at NLS Legal, our multi-award-winning-teaching law firm, the only on-campus law firm at a UK Law School. Our School has built a reputation for excellence in the provision of legal education and in shaping the careers of solicitors, barristers and legal practitioners at both national and international levels. In addition to our outstanding research expertise, we have long established links with policy makers, professional bodies and leading law firms, including a growing number of significant international associations. We have an extensive record of delivering excellent bespoke training programmes for practitioners and professional bodies, and have strengths in commissioned research, both in the UK and overseas. For any informal queries about the role or the team, please contact Associate Professor Dr Emma Ireton emma.ireton@ntu.ac.uk Join Us 30 - 35 days annual leave per year plus statutory bank holidays and 5 university closure days pro rata Hybrid working - we encourage and offer a mixture of office working and working from home. You're empowered to define how you work best for the benefits of your stakeholders. Flexibility - take ownership over how you get your work done. We're open to different working patterns and approaches. Salary Sacrifice Retirement Savings Plan with life assurance and income protection. Available to colleagues who choose to opt out of the contractual pension scheme. Minimum colleague contributions of 0% matched with minimum NTU contributions of 8%. Access to a wealth of formal and informal professional development opportunities to develop your skills and advance your career. Range of health and wellbeing services, including a Health Cash Plan, voluntary benefits, discounts, and savings for all colleagues. And a whole lot more\u2026Find out more about the range of benefits we offer. Come and be part of our success. Apply today. Safe and Inclusive At NTU, we continue to build an inclusive culture that encourages, supports and celebrates the diverse voices and experiences of our students and colleagues. By championing positive wellbeing, we promote an environment where all can thrive and reach their full potential. We welcome the unique contributions that you can bring and we encourage people from underrepresented communities and backgrounds to apply to join our team. Please note that unfortunately, this role has been assessed as ineligible for sponsorship under the UK Visas & Immigration points-based immigration system however, we recommend that you assess your eligibility before applying for this position. For more information visit the Government Skilled Worker visa support page. However, applications are welcome from candidates who do not currently have the right to work in the UK, but who would be eligible to obtain a valid visa via another route. Please consult the Home Office website for further information. Please note that this role is covered by the Rehabilitation of Offenders Act (1974) and successful applicants will be asked to declare any unspent criminal convictions. Take a look around the company https://www.ntu.ac.uk/ Apply for job favorite_border Save this job Go to main site Terms & Conditions Accessibility Nottingham Trent University\u00a0applicant tracking system delivered and supported by Jobtrain"}, "https://vacancies.ntu.ac.uk/Job/JobDetail?JobId=2597": {"title": "School Research Administrator", "description": "NTU | Jobs | Search here for your perfect career - Job Information  | Apply for School Research Administrator Cookie Policy By clicking \"Allow Cookies\", you agree to the storing of cookies on your device to analyse site usage, and assist in our marketing efforts. Cookie Policy (Opens in a new tab) Decline Allow cookies Skip to main content List Vacancies (current) Sign in Accessibility Tools List Vacancies (current) Back to Search Results School Research Administrator Apply for job Job reference: 552562 Location: City Campus Employment type: Fixed Term Contract Team: NBS School Office Closing date: 06/11/2026 School / Directorate: Nottingham Business School Salary / Grade Grade E (\u00a328,063 - \u00a330,185 p.a. pro rata) Where to find us location_on Get directions Empower Future Leaders. Doing things differently. School Research Administrator Salary- \u00a328,063 - \u00a330,185 per annum (pro rata) This is a part time role (6 hours a day, 4 days a week)/ Fixed term for 1 year About the Role We have an exciting opportunity to join the School Management Support Team at Nottingham Business School as a part-time School Research Administrator (24 hours per week) . This is a one-year fixed-term role supporting the School's thriving research community and contributing to the delivery of a professional, efficient and high-quality administration service. The role will be based at our City Campus and will involve a mix of on-campus and remote home working. As a School Research Administrator, you will provide comprehensive administrative support to the Heads of Research Centres and work with Research Centre staff to ensure effective administration of our Research Groups. You will play a key role in the organisation and administration of research programmes, acting as a central point of contact for academic colleagues, research students and a range of internal and external stakeholders. A commitment to delivering excellent customer service and support is essential. The role offers a varied workload and will involve supporting research events and training activities, managing research student administration processes, coordinating meetings and committees, maintaining records and databases, and liaising with colleagues across the University, including the Doctoral School. You will also contribute to activities that support the School's research objectives, accreditation activity and postgraduate research experience. Please submit a supporting statement of no more than 1,000 words demonstrating how you meet the requirements of the School Research Administrator role. For more details, please take a look at the role profile. We'll still consider applications even if you don't meet every single one of the requirements, so don't be put off if you don't match them perfectly. Interview Date: w/c 16th November 2026 About Us Nottingham Business School (NBS) delivers research and education that combine academic excellence with real-world impact on people, business, and society. We lead in experiential learning and personalised education, and our research drives positive change across social and economic spheres. This informs all our programmes, from undergraduate to doctoral. With strong partnerships across business, public, and voluntary sectors, NBS is known as the business school for business . We hold the prestigious Triple Crown Accreditation (EQUIS, AACSB, AMBA), placing us in the top 1% of business schools worldwide. Discover more on our website . At NTU, we do things differently. Join one of Europe\u2019s largest and most innovative business schools to help shape inclusive research and make a real difference. For any informal queries about the role or the team, please contact John Moore (School Coordinator) at john.moore@ntu.ac.uk. Join Us Hybrid working - We support flexible ways of working through a combination of campus-based and home working where applicable. For full-time roles, this includes a minimum of 60% on-campus commitment. We trust colleagues to work with their teams to shape working patterns that enable them to deliver the best possible outcomes for their stakeholders. Flexibility - We welcome and support a range of working patterns and approaches, helping colleagues balance their work and personal commitments while meeting the needs of the role. 28 - 30 days annual leave, plus statutory bank holidays and 5 university closure days pro rata. Salary Sacrifice Retirement Savings Plan with life assurance and income protection. Available to colleagues who choose to opt out of the contractual pension scheme. Minimum colleague contributions of 0% matched with minimum NTU contributions of 8%. Range of health and wellbeing services, including a Health Cash Plan, voluntary benefits, discounts, and savings for all colleagues. Access to a wealth of formal and informal professional development opportunities to develop your skills and advance your career. We are committed to advancing Equality, Diversity and Inclusion across all areas of our work. We actively promote a culture of respect and belonging and we welcome applications from people of all backgrounds. For more information please click here - Equality, Diversity and Inclusion | Nottingham Trent University And a whole lot more\u2026Find out more about the range of benefits we offer. Come and be part of our success. Apply today. Safe and Inclusive At NTU, we continue to build an inclusive culture that encourages, supports and celebrates the diverse voices and experiences of our students and colleagues. By championing positive wellbeing, we promote an environment where all can thrive and reach their full potential. We welcome the unique contributions that you can bring and we encourage people from underrepresented communities and backgrounds to apply to join our team. Please note that unfortunately, this role has been assessed as ineligible for sponsorship under the UK Visas & Immigration points-based immigration system however, we recommend that you assess your eligibility before applying for this position. For more information visit the Government Skilled Worker visa support page. However, applications are welcome from candidates who do not currently have the right to work in the UK, but who would be eligible to obtain a valid visa via another route. Please consult the Home Office website for further information. Please note that this role is covered by the Rehabilitation of Offenders Act (1974) and successful applicants will be asked to declare any unspent criminal convictions. Supporting Documents save_alt JDPS- School Research Administrator (PDF, KB) Take a look around the company https://www.ntu.ac.uk/ Apply for job favorite_border Save this job Go to main site Terms & Conditions Accessibility Nottingham Trent University\u00a0applicant tracking system delivered and supported by Jobtrain"}, "https://vacancies.ntu.ac.uk/Job/JobDetail?JobId=2678": {"title": "Lecturer / Senior Lecturer in Forensics Science", "description": "NTU | Jobs | Search here for your perfect career - Job Information  | Apply for Lecturer / Senior Lecturer in Forensics Science Skip to main content List Vacancies (current) Sign in Accessibility Tools List Vacancies (current) Back to Search Results Lecturer / Senior Lecturer in Forensics Science Apply for job Job reference: 552643 Location: Clifton Campus Employment type: Fixed Term Contract Team: Chemistry and Forensics Closing date: 28/10/2026 School / Directorate: School of Science and Technology Salary / Grade HE Lecturer or Senior Lecturer (\u00a339,984 - \u00a358,624 pa pro rata) Where to find us location_on Get directions Diverse community. Inclusive Research. Rewarding Careers. Doing things differently. Lecturer/ Senior Lecturer in Forensics Science Lecturer Salary- \u00a339,984- \u00a343,671 per annum Senior Lecturer Salary- \u00a346,320- \u00a358,624 per annum Full time/ Fixed term for 9 months About the Role The Department of Physical Sciences is seeking to appoint an enthusiastic and ambitious Lecturer or Senior Lecturer in Forensic Science to join our thriving academic community on a fixed-term basis for nine months. This is an exciting opportunity to contribute to the delivery and continued development of our accredited undergraduate and postgraduate forensic science programmes while advancing your own research, scholarship, or professional practice. We are looking for a passionate educator who can inspire students through innovative, evidence-based teaching and provide an outstanding learning experience. You will contribute to teaching, assessment and curriculum development, across our forensic science portfolio, while also supporting teaching more broadly within the department. We welcome applications from candidates with academic, industrial, or practitioner backgrounds. We are particularly interested in individuals with expertise in one or more of the following areas: Marks and traces evidence The English legal system and the role of forensic science within criminal justice ISO standards and quality management within forensic practice Forensic biology You will join a collaborative team of experienced practitioners and academics committed to delivering an excellent student experience and maintaining high professional standards. Our forensic science programmes are recognised among the top-performing in the UK (Complete University Guide), providing students with a strong blend of scientific knowledge, practical skills, and professional relevance. The successful candidate will demonstrate a proactive and collegiate approach, a commitment to educational excellence, and the ability to contribute to the continued growth and success of the subject area. Whether you are an established academic seeking your next challenge or a forensic professional looking to transition into higher education, we would welcome your application. This nine-month fixed-term appointment offers an excellent opportunity to join a supportive and high-performing team and help shape the next generation of forensic scientists. For more details, please take a look at the role profile. We'll still consider applications even if you don't meet every single one of the requirements, so don't be put off if you don't match them perfectly. To ensure the diverse needs of our team are met we actively encourage secondments and offer flexible part-time working patterns - we're focused on finding the right person for the role. Interview Date: w/c 9th November 2026 About Us The School of Science and Technology at Nottingham Trent University (NTU) is an exciting multidisciplinary environment for learning, teaching and research, with some of the best facilities in the UK. We pride ourselves on delivering high-quality teaching and diverse, real-world research. We specialise in biosciences, chemistry, computing and technology, as well as engineering, forensic science, mathematics, physics and sport science. This mix of traditional and modern subjects encourages and inspires future innovators. Our industry-standard Forensic Science facilities and equipment support our teaching and research and they are also used regularly by external organisations. Our crime scene training facility is one of the largest in the UK and is regularly used for teaching, training and research. For any informal queries about the role or the team, please contact Emma Rixon (Head of Department) at emma.rixon@ntu.ac.uk. Join Us Find out more about our academic community at NTU, including the support we offer to academics at all stages of their careers. We also offer: Hybrid working - We support flexible ways of working through a combination of campus-based and home working where applicable. For full-time roles, this includes a minimum of 60% on-campus commitment. We trust colleagues to work with their teams to shape working patterns that enable them to deliver the best possible outcomes for their stakeholders. Flexibility - We welcome and support a range of working patterns and approaches, helping colleagues balance their work and personal commitments while meeting the needs of the role. 30 - 35 days annual leave per year plus statutory bank holidays and 5 university closure days pro rata Salary Sacrifice Retirement Savings Plan with life assurance and income protection. Available to colleagues who choose to opt out of the contractual pension scheme. Minimum colleague contributions of 0% matched with minimum NTU contributions of 8%. Opportunity to receive a bonus for exceptional performance and contribution Range of health and wellbeing services, including a Health Cash Plan, voluntary benefits, discounts, and savings for all colleagues. We are committed to advancing Equality, Diversity and Inclusion across all areas of our work. We actively promote a culture of respect and belonging and we welcome applications from people of all backgrounds. For more information please click here - Equality, Diversity and Inclusion | Nottingham Trent University And a whole lot more\u2026Find out more about the range of benefits we offer. Come and be part of our success. Apply today. Safe and Inclusive At NTU, we continue to build an inclusive culture that encourages, supports and celebrates the diverse voices and experiences of our students and colleagues. By championing positive wellbeing, we promote an environment where all can thrive and reach their full potential. We welcome the unique contributions that you can bring and we encourage people from underrepresented communities and backgrounds to apply to join our team. Depending on your individual circumstances this role may be eligible for sponsorship under the UKVI Skilled Worker route. We recommend that you review your individual circumstances before applying, or for more information visit the Government Skilled Worker visa support page. This role is covered by the Rehabilitation of Offenders Act (1974) and successful applicants will be asked to declare any unspent criminal convictions. Take a look around the company https://www.ntu.ac.uk/ Apply for job favorite_border Save this job Go to main site Terms & Conditions Accessibility Nottingham Trent University\u00a0applicant tracking system delivered and supported by Jobtrain"}}, "rows": {"https://vacancies.ntu.ac.uk/Job/JobDetail?JobId=1223": {"school_id": 1871, "posting_url": "https://vacancies.ntu.ac.uk/Job/JobDetail?JobId=1223", "job_title_in_post": "Associate Dean, Research", "position_type": "Assistant_Professor; Associate_Professor; Full_Professor", "job_term": "Full-time", "department_or_school": "School of Science and Technology", "area_key_words": "Research; University strategic; motivating staff", "deadline_of_application": "15/11/2026", "position_start_date": ""}, "https://vacancies.ntu.ac.uk/Job/JobDetail?JobId=2587": {"school_id": 1871, "posting_url": "https://vacancies.ntu.ac.uk/Job/JobDe